hadiths[182]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3992","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, and Musa bin Al-Hasan bin Abbad told us, they said: Affan bin Muslim, Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When God formed Adam He left him, and Satan started walking around him and looking at him, and when he saw that he was hollow, he said: I have overtaken him with a character that cannot be controlled. “This is an authentic hadith on the condition that A Muslim, and they did not produce it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3992 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"3993","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Nadr Al-Azdi told me, Muawiyah bin Amr told us, Zaydah told us, Ammar bin Abi Muawiyah Al-Bajli narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “Adam did not inhabit Paradise except between “Asr prayer until sunset.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3993 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"3994","Ahmad ibn Yaqoub al-Thaqafi told me, Musa ibn Harun told me, Amr ibn Ali told me, Imran ibn Uyaynah told me, Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib informed me, about Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: “Indeed, the first time God sent Adam down to the land of India,” this is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3994 - True"
"3995","Muhammad bin Al-Hasan Al-Karazi told us, Ali bin Abdul-Aziz told us, Hajjaj bin Minhal told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Yusuf bin Mahran, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: Ali bin Abi Talib said: “The best wind on earth is India, where Adam was descended.” May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, and its trees became suspended from the scent of Paradise.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3995 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"3996","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl told us, Hawdha bin Khalifa told us, Awf told us, on the authority of Qasamah bin Zuhair, on the authority of Abi Bakr bin Abi Musa Al-Ash’ari said: “When God brought Adam out of Paradise, He provided him with the fruits of Paradise and taught him how to make everything.” “These fruits of yours are among the fruits of Paradise, but some have changed and some have not changed.” The chain of transmission is authentic, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3996 - True"
"3997","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Amr Al-Ahmasi informed us of Kufa, Al-Hussein bin Al-Rabi’ told us, Hammad bin Al-Sari told us, Abu Bakr bin told us Ayyash, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that the Jews came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and asked him Regarding the creation of the heavens and the earth, he said: “God created the earth on Sunday and Monday, and God created the mountains on Tuesday and all the benefits that are in them. On Wednesday, He created the trees, the water, the cities, the buildings, and the ruins. These are four. Then God Almighty said: “Indeed, you will disbelieve in Him. He created the earth in two days, and you will make equals to Him. That is the Lord of the worlds, and He has placed therein mountains above them, and He has blessed therein, and He has decreed therein its sustenance in four days, equal to those who ask. And on Thursday He created the heaven, and on Friday He created the stars, the sun, the moon, and the angels until Three hours remained of it, so in the first of these three hours He created the appointed hours when whoever dies, and in the second He cast the blight on everything. That which benefits people, and in the third day Adam made him dwell in Paradise, and commanded Iblis to prostrate to him, and expelled him from it in the last hour.” Then The Jews said: Then what, Muhammad? He said: “Then He sat on the throne.” They said: You have been correct if you had completed it. They said: Then he rested. He said: Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, became angry. severe, so it was revealed {And indeed We created the heavens and the earth and all that is between them in six days, and no deceit has touched Us, so be patient over what they say} “This is a hadith The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3997 - Abu Saeed Al-Baqal said Ibn Ma’in does not write his hadith"
"3998","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl told us, Sa’id bin Suleiman Al-Wasiti told us, Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Orouba, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Utai Al-Saadi, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, who said: “Adam was a tall man with many hairs on his head as if it were “Nakhla Suhuq” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3998 - True"
"3999","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan told us, Muhammad bin Bishr Al-Abdi told us, Muhammad bin Amr told us, on the authority of Abi Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The best day on which the sun rises is Friday, the creation of Adam.” “In it, and in it He was descended to the earth.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and he narrated it from the hadith of Al-Zuhri without this wording.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3999 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4000","Abd al-Samad bin Ali bin Mukarram told us, in Baghdad, Ja`far bin Muhammad al-Sayegh told us, al-Hasan bin Muhammad al-Marwazi told us, Jarir bin Hazim told us, On the authority of Kulthum ibn Jabr, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “God took The covenant came from Adam through Naaman, meaning Arafat, so he took out from his loins all the offspring that he had and scattered them before him like atom, then He spoke to them before and said: “Am I not your Lord?” They said, “Yes, we bear witness, lest you say so on the Day of Resurrection.” [Al-A’raf: 172] to his saying, “Because the invalids have done.” [Al-A’raf: 173] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4000 - True"
"4001","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih and Abu Al-Hasan Al-Anazi told us, saying: Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Al-Qanabi told us, and Yahya bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Zayd bin Abi Anisa, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid bin Abd al-Rahman bin Zayd bin al-Khattab, on the authority of Muslim bin Yasar al-Juhani, that Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, was asked about this verse: “And when your Lord took from the children of Adam from their backs their offspring” [Al-A’raf: 172] Omar bin Al-Khattab said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “God created Adam, then wiped his back with his right hand, and extracted from it offspring and said: I created these for Paradise and for the deeds of the people of Paradise they will do. Then he wiped his back and produced offspring from him and said: I created “These people are for the Fire, and they do the work of the people of the Fire.” Then a man said: O Messenger of God, what is the work? He said: “Indeed, when God creates a servant for Paradise, He uses him to do the work of the people of Paradise until he dies doing the work of the people of Paradise, and he enters Paradise. “The servant was created for Hell. He used him with the work of the people of Hell until he died doing the work of the people of Hell and then he entered Hell.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it was not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4001 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4002","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan told us, Al-Hasan bin Atiya told us, Al-Hasan bin Salih told us, on the authority of Al-Minhal Ibn Amr, on the authority of Saeed Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both. Then Adam received words from his Lord and He turned to him. He said: O Lord, pain Do you create me with your own hand? He said: “Yes.” He said: O Lord, did you not breathe into me of your Spirit? He said: “Yes.” He said: O Lord, have you not made me dwell in Your Paradise? He said: “Yes.” He said: O Lord, has not your mercy preceded your wrath? He said: “Yes.” He said: Do you think that if I repent and amend, you will be returned to Paradise? He said: “Yes.” He said: It is his saying {So Adam received words from his Lord} [Al-Baqarah: 37] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4002 - True"
"4003","Ahmad bin Uthman bin Yahya Al-Adami, the reciter in Baghdad, told us, Abu Qalaba told us, Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith told us, Omar bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah ibn Jundub, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Eve was without a child. So she vowed that if a son lived to her, she would name him Abd al-Harith. Then a son lived to her, so she named him Abd al-Harith. But that was only by revelation from Satan: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4003 - True"
"4004","Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan bin Ayyub told us, Abu Hatim Al-Razi told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit Al-Bunani, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Utai ibn Damrah, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “When Adam died, the angels washed him with water.” And they insisted on it and said: This is the tradition of Adam regarding his son. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4004 - True"
"4005","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Ahmasi told us, Al-Hasan bin Humaid bin Al-Rabi’ told us, Musa bin Ismail, and Hadba bin Khaled told us, They said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Yusuf bin Mahran, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “God sent Noah for forty years, and he remained among his people for a thousand years, minus fifty years, calling upon them, and he lived after the flood for sixty years until The people increased and dispersed.” The two sheikhs agreed on the hadith of Abu Hurairah and Anas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the hadith of intercession. “So they would go to Noah.” They say: You are the first messenger sent to earth.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4005 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4006","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ghayath Al-Abdi told us, Ja’far bin Abi Uthman Al-Tayalisi told us, Ayyash bin Al-Walid Al-Raqam told us, Abdul-Ala, Saeed bin Abi Arouba told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, on the authority of Samurah bin Jundub, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Noah begot three sons, Shem, Ham, and Japheth, the father of the Romans.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4006 - True"
"4007","Muhammad bin Yusuf al-Daqiqi told me, Muhammad bin Imran al-Nasawi told me, Ahmad bin Zuhair told us, Waki` bin al-Jarrah told us, on the authority of Hamza al-Zayat, on the authority of Adi Ibn Thabit, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: “The master of the prophets is five, and Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, is the master of The five: Noah, Abraham, Moses, Jesus, and Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon them. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of transmission, even if it is attributed to my father.” kitten
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4007 - True"
"4008","Ali bin Issa Al-Hairi told me, Musaddad bin Qatn told us, Uthman bin Abi Shaybah told us, Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Labiba, and he is Muhammad bin Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, that he mentioned the words of God Almighty: {Indeed, We sent Noah to his people} [Noah: 1], so he mentioned """" That Noah took a bath and saw his son looking at him, so he said: Look at me while I wash. May God bless your color. He said: Fasud, so he is Abu Al-Sudan. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4008 - Muhammad bin Abi Labiba said: They have weakened him"
"4009","Abu Nasr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Omar Al-Khafaf told me, Ahmad bin Salama told us, Muhammad bin Bashar told us, Abu Dawud told us, Hammam told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, said: “Between Noah and Adam there were ten generations, all of them following a law of truth. Then they disagreed, so God sent the prophets as bringers of good tidings and warnings.” He said: Likewise, in Abdullah’s recitation, “The people were one community, but they differed.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4009 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"4010","Ali bin Abdul Rahman bin Mani told us, Ahmad bin Hazim told us, on the authority of Abu Gharza, Musa bin Yaqoub al-Zam’i told us, Faid, Mawla Ubaid told us God Ibn Ali said that Ibrahim Ibn Abd al-Rahman Ibn Abi Rabi’ah told him that Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, told him The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If God had had mercy on one of Noah’s people, he would have had mercy on the boy’s mother.” The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “ Noah stayed among his people for a thousand years minus fifty years, calling them to God until it was the end of his time. He planted a tree and it became great and all the trees went away. Then he cut it off, then he started building a ship, and they mocked him and said: He is building a ship on land, so how will it sail? He said: It will You know, when he finished, the oven gushed and the water poured into the dishes. The boy’s mother was afraid for him, and she loved him very much, so she went out to the mountain. Until it reached a third of it, and when the water reached it, it went out with it until it reached two-thirds of the mountain, and when it reached it, it went out until it came to rest on the mountain, and when it reached The water hit her neck, and she lifted him with her hand until the water carried him away. If God had mercy on one of them, he would have had mercy on the boy’s mother. “This hadith has an authentic chain of narration and did not He brings him out.”"
"4011","Abu Saeed Al-Ahmasi told me, in Kufa, Al-Hussein bin Humaid bin Al-Rabi’ told us, Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Sulami told us, Muhammad bin Hassan told us, Muhammad ibn Ja`far al-Sadiq, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, said: “Our Lord Almighty gathered for Noah the knowledge of all the past. And he supported him with a spirit of his own, and he called on his people secretly and publicly for nine hundred and fifty years. Whenever a century passed, a century followed it, so he increased their disbelief. “And tyranny.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4011 - True"
"4012","Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Baraa told us, Abd Al-Munim bin Idris told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Wahb Ibn Munabbih said: Al-Hassan Ibn Abi Al-Hassan mentioned on the authority of seven people who witnessed Badr. Wahb said: Abdullah Ibn Abbas narrated to me They all reported the hadith to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “On the Day of Resurrection, God will call Noah and his people to be the first of people, and he will say: What Did you answer Noah? So they say: He did not call us, nor did we inform us, nor did we advise us, nor did we command, nor forbid us. So Noah says: O Lord, I called them with a widespread supplication among the ancients and the last. Nation after nation until he reached the Seal of the Prophets, Ahmad, and abrogated it, read it, believed in it, and believed in it. Then God says to the angels: Call on Ahmad. And his nation, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his nation come, their light running before them, and Noah says to Muhammad and his nation: Do you know? Indeed, I conveyed the message to my people, and I strove to give them advice, and I strove to save them from the fire, secretly and openly, but my supplication only increased them. Fleeing? Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him and his nation, says: “For we bear witness, by what you have called upon us, that you are truthful in everything you have said.” Then Noah’s people would say: And where did you learn this, O Ahmad? You and your nation, and we were the first of the nations, and you and your nation are the last of the nations? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: “In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. Indeed, We sent Noah to his people, saying, ‘Warn your people before There will come to them a painful punishment.} [Noah: 1] He recited the Surah until he completed it, and when he completed it, his nation said, “We bear witness that this is the true story and what There is no god but God, and indeed God is the Mighty, the Wise. God Almighty says at that time: “Distinguish yourself today, O criminals. “The first to excel in Hell.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4012 - Its chain of transmission is weak"
"4013","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Hisham bin Ali Al-Sadusi told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Dawud bin Abi Al-Furat told us, Alba bin Ahmar told us, On the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that he recited this verse: {And do not display yourselves like the display of the times of pre-Islamic times} [Al-Ahzab: 33] He said: “There were a thousand years between Noah and Idris, and there were two generations of Adam’s offspring, one of whom inhabited the plain, and the other inhabited the mountain.” And the men of the mountain were in the morning, and on the women there was a dimple, and the women of the plain were in the morning, and on the men there was a dimple, and that Satan went to a man from the people of The plain in the form of the shepherds’ boy, and he came in it with a voice the likes of which the people had never heard, so they celebrated a festival to which they gathered every year, and a man from The people of the mountain attacked them while they were on that holiday, and he saw the women and their morning, so he came to his companions and told them about that, so they turned To them and they descended with them, and the indecency among them became apparent. That is the saying of God Almighty: {And do not display yourselves like the display of the times of pre-Islamic times} [Al-Ahzab: 33].”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4013 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4014","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Isfaraini informed us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Baraa told us, Abd Al-Munim bin Idris informed us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Wahb bin Munabbih said that he was asked about Idris, who is he and at what time was he? He said: “He is the grandfather of Noah, who is called Khanukh, and he is alive in Paradise.” Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Yassar said: “Idris was the first of the sons of Adam.” He was given prophecy, and he is Enoch bin Yazid bin Ahlaleel bin Qinan bin Nashir bin Seth bin Adam.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4014 - Abdel Moneim bin Idris, Ahmed’s lie"
"4015","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Ahmasi told me about Kufa, Al-Hussein bin Humaid bin Al-Rabi’ told us, Marwan bin Ja’far Al-Samari told us, Humaid told us Ibn Muadh Al-Yashkari, Mudarrak Ibn Abdul-Rahman Al-Anazi told us, Al-Hussein Ibn Dhakwan told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan Al-Basri, on the authority of Samurah Ibn Jundub, He said: “Then the Prophet of God, Idris, was a tall white man, with a large belly, a broad chest, little body hair, and a large head of hair. One of his eyes was larger than the other, and there were three white spots on his chest without leprosy. When God saw of the people of the earth what he saw of Because of their injustice and transgression against the command of God, God raised him to the sixth heaven, where he is. He says: “And We raised him to a high place” [Maryam: 57]
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4015 - Its chain of transmission is dark and cannot be supported by evidence"
"4016","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Battah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm Al-Tamimi told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad told us Ibn Omar Al-Waqidi, Shurayh Ibn Yazid told me, on the authority of Ibrahim Ibn Muhammad Ibn Ziyad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Busr, he said: He put The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, placed his hand on my head and said: “This boy will live for a century.” He said: He lived for a hundred years. Al-Waqidi said: God says: God Almighty {And many centuries between that} [Al-Furqan: 38] So there were ten centuries between Noah and Adam, and between him and Abraham ten centuries, so Abraham was born. God’s friend is at the beginning of two thousand years of Adam’s creation.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4016 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4017","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Jarir told us, about Amara Ibn Al-Qaqa’, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “And they say: O Abraham, You are the friend of the Most Gracious. The people of the heavens and the earth have heard of your conceit. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4017 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4018","Ahmad bin Salman Al-Faqih told us in Baghdad, Hilal bin Al-Ala’ Al-Ruqi told us, Abdullah bin Jaafar told us, Ubayd Allah bin Amr told us, on the authority of Zaid Ibn Abi Anisa, on the authority of Amr Ibn Murrah, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Al-Harith, he said: Jundub told us, that he heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, say before That he died: “Indeed, God has taken me as a friend just as He took Abraham as a friend.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4018 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4019","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Ahmad bin Busr al-Marthadi told us, Yahya bin Ma’in told us, Hisham bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that when the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw the pictures in the house, he did not He entered, until he ordered it to be erased, and he saw Abraham and Ishmael with the cuts in their hands, and he said: “God will fight them, and by God, if they divide “With sharp arrows, never.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4019 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"4020","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, he said: “And Ibrahim, Khalil al-Rahman, his successor and prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, the son of Azar bin Majur bin Saruh bin Rau bin Maleh bin Aber bin Salikh ibn Arfakhshadh ibn Shem ibn Noah, may God’s prayers be upon him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4020 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4021","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Isfaraini informed us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Baraa informed us, Al-Mu’afia bin Sulayman Al-Harrani informed us, Muhammad bin Salamah Al-Harrani, on the authority of Abu Abdul-Rahim Al-Harrani, on the authority of Abu Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Abu Umamah, he said: “A palm appeared from the sky between On two of her fingers there was a white hair, so she started to approach Ibrahim’s head, then she approached and threw it on his head, and said: Ignite. Dignified, then God inspired him to purify himself, and he was the first to become young and circumcised, and God revealed to Abraham what was revealed to Muhammad in the Qur’an. So it was in what God revealed to him: “The repentant, the worshipers, the thankful, the wanderers, the ones who kneel and prostrate, those who enjoin what is right and forbid what is wrong.” And those who maintain the limits of God, and give good tidings to the believers} [At-Tawbah: 112] and {Indeed, the believers have succeeded} [Al-Mu’minun: 1] to His saying: {Those who will inherit Paradise. They will abide therein forever.} [Al-Mu’minun: 11] And those in the Ahzab {Indeed, the Muslim men and Muslim women} [Al-Ahzab: 35] until the end of the verse, and the one in Ask {those They will perpetually adhere to their prayers} [Al-Ma’arij: 23] until His saying, “And those who stand by their testimonies” [Al-Ma’arij: 33] And none of these arrows were fulfilled except “Ibrahim, the friend of God and Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon them and his family.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4021 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4022","Abdullah bin Ishaq Al-Baghawi told us in Baghdad, Al-Hasan bin Makram Al-Bazzaz told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, On the authority of Yahya bin Saeed Al-Ansari, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, that Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, said: “Ibrahim, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was circumcised. He passed away after one hundred and twenty years of arrival, and he died when he was two hundred years old.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4022 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4023","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Tamim bin Muhammad narrated to us, and another time Abu Saeed Al-Ahmasi narrated to us, Al-Hussein bin Humaid bin Al-Rabi’, they said: Uthman bin Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, he said: “Abraham was circumcised one hundred and twenty years after his arrival, and after that he lived for eighty years.”"
"4024","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Humaid bin Ayyash Al-Ramli told us, Ma’mal bin Ismail told us, Sufyan Al-Thawri told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Haritha bin Mudarib, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, said: “When Abraham, peace be upon him, was ordered to build the House, Ismail and Hagar went out with him, and when He came to Mecca and saw on his head in the place of the House something like a cloud in it like a head. He spoke to him and said: O Abraham, build on my shadow or According to my destiny, and do not increase or subtract. When he had built it, he set out and succeeded Ishmael and Hagar. This is where God Almighty says: {And when We appointed for Abraham The place of the House is that you do not associate anything with Me, and purify My House for those who circle around, and those who stand and those who kneel and prostrate.” [Al-Hajj: 26] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and it has not He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4024 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4025","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Sinan Al-Qazzaz told us, Abu Ali Ubayd Allah bin Abdul Majeed Al-Hanafi told us, he said: I heard Kathir bin Kathir, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: “Ibrahim, peace and blessings be upon him, came and found Ismail was repairing a house for him behind Zamzam, so Abraham said to him: O Ismail, your Lord has commanded me to build the house. So Ishmael said to him: So obey your Lord in what He commands you. He said: So I mean it. He said: So he stood up with him and made Abraham build it and Ishmael handing him the stones and saying: {Our Lord, accept it from us. Indeed, You are the Hearer, the Knower} [Al-Baqarah: 127] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4025 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4026","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: “When Abraham built the House, God inspired him to announce the Hajj to the people. He said: So Abraham said: Indeed, your Lord has taken a house and commanded you to perform Hajj to it, but whatever stone, tree, or hill he heard responded to him. Or dust: At your service, O God, at your command. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4026 - True"
"4027","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl informed us, Yahya bin Abi Talib informed us, Abdul Wahhab bin Abdul Majeed informed us, Dawud bin Abi informed us Hind, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “Islam is thirty arrows, and he has never been tested with this religion but established it.” Abraham, peace and blessings be upon him. God Almighty said: “And Abraham is the one who paid back” [Al-Najm: 37]. So God recorded for him an escape from the Fire. “This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4027 - True"
"4028","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, he said: Al-Thawri told me, On the authority of Abu Ishaq Al-Hamdani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Khalil, he said: I heard Ali saying: “A man asked forgiveness for his parents while they were polytheists.” So I said: Do you ask forgiveness for them while they are polytheists? He said: Abraham asked forgiveness for his father, so I mentioned that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and God revealed: {And what was Abraham’s request for forgiveness for his father? Except for the promise he promised her} [At-Tawbah: 114]
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4028 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4029","Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan bin Ayyub told us, Abu Yahya bin Abi Masarra told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir Al-Hazami told us, Abdul Aziz told me Ibn Imran, Ismail Ibn Ibrahim Ibn Abi Habiba told me, on the authority of Dawud Ibn al-Husayn, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him. About them, he said: “He was the first to speak Arabic and write a book according to its pronunciation and logic, then he made a single book like In the Name of God, the Most Gracious “The Most Merciful, the One who is connected until his son Ismail bin Ibrahim, may God’s prayers be upon them, separated him.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4029 - Abdul Aziz bin Imran Wah"
"4030","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmed bin Muhammad bin Issa Al-Qadi told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Al-Duha, I think it was on the authority of Stolen, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Every prophet has guardians from among the prophets, and my guardian and friend is my father.” Abraham.” Then he recited, “Indeed, the people closest to Abraham are those who followed him.” [Al Imran: 68]
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4030 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4031","Abu Abdullah bin Battah told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, Al-Thawri told me, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Indeed, every prophet has governors from among the prophets, and My guardian and my friend, among them is my father Ibrahim. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recited {Indeed, the people closest to Abraham} [Al Imran: 68] “until the end of the verse” hadith If Abu Nu`aym combines it with the hadith of al-Waqidi, it is correct, for it must be stolen.”"
"4032","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Ziyad told us, Ibrahim bin Musa told us, Hisham bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ibn Ka’b ibn Malik, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When you conquer Egypt, strive “It is better for the Copts, for they have protection and kinship.” Al-Zuhri said: “The kinship is that the mother of Ishmael is among them.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and it was not He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4032 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4033","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Ahmasi told us about Kufa, Al-Hussein bin Humaid told us, Marwan bin Ja’far Al-Samari told us, Humaid bin Muadh told us, Mudrak bin Abdul Rahman told me, Al-Hussein bin Dhakwan told me, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, on the authority of Ka’b, he said: “Ismail bin Ibrahim was The Prophet of God whom he called True to His Promise, and he was a man of sharpness who struggled with the enemies of God and God gave him victory over them and victory, and he was strong. The war against the infidels does not fear for God’s sake the blame of a mean person, small-headed, thick-necked, long-handed and long-legged, who strikes with his hands. his knees, and he is standing, with small eyes, a long nose, broad shoulders, long fingers, an outstanding character, strong, severe, and violent towards disbelievers, and he commanded his family to pray and give zakat, and he was well-pleased with his Lord.” He said: “and his zakat was an offering to God from Their wealth, and he did not promise anything to anyone unless he fulfilled it, so God called him True to His Promise, and he was a Messenger and a Prophet.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4033 - Its chain of transmission is weak"
"4034","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Yahya bin Ma’in told us, Yahya bin Al-Yaman told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of A statement, on the authority of Al-Shabi, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “The sacrificed Ishmael.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4034 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4035","Abu Muhammad Al-Muzani told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hadrami told us, Al-Hasan bin Hammad told us, Abdul Rahman bin Suleiman told us, on the authority of Israel, On the authority of Thuwayr bin Abi Fakhta, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, “And We ransomed him with a great sacrifice” [Al-Saffat: 107] He said: Ismail When Abraham slaughtered the ram
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4035 - Thawair bin Abi Fakhta. Wah"
"4036","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shafi’i told us, Ubaid bin Hatim Al-Hafiz Al-Ijli told us, Ismail bin Ubaid bin Omar bin Abi told us Karima Al-Harrani, Abdul Rahim Al-Khattati told us, Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Utbi told us, Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Sanabihi told us, he said: We attended a council Muawiyah bin Abi Sufyan, then the people remembered Ishmael and Ishaq bin Ibrahim, and some of them said: The sacrificed one is Ishmael, and some of them said: Rather. Ishaq the sacrifice, and Muawiyah said: “You fell for the expert. We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Bedouins came to him and said: O Messenger of God, I left the country dry and the water dry, the wealth perished and the children lost, so repay me with what God has repaid you, O son of the two sacrifices. Then the Messenger of God smiled. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he was not denounced. So we said: O Commander of the Faithful, what are the two sacrifices? He said: When Abdul-Muttalib was ordered to dig Zamzam, he vowed to God, if God facilitated his command, to slaughter some of his sons, so he brought them out, so he contributed. Between them, the arrow went out to Abdullah, and he wanted to slaughter him, but his maternal uncles from Banu Makhzum prevented him, and they said: Please your Lord and redeem your son. He said: He ransomed him with a hundred she-camels. He said: He is the one who was sacrificed and Ismail the Second.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4036 - Its chain of transmission is weak"
"4037","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr Al-Khawlani told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Omar bin Qais told me, on the authority of Ata Ibn Abi Rabah, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that he said: “The redeemed is Ishmael, and the Jews claimed that he was Isaac.” And the Jews lied.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4037 - Ibn Wahb heard it from him, meaning from Omar bin Qays, and he perished."
"4038","Abdul Rahman bin Al-Hasan Al-Qadi told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shu’bah told us, and Muhammad bin Musa told me Al-Faqih, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, Ja’far told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Bayan, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him. On the authority of them, he said about the one whom God ransomed with a great sacrifice, he said: “He is Ishmael.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4038 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4039","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, he said: I heard Muhammad Ibn Ka'b Al-Qurazi says: “The one whom God commanded Abraham to slaughter was one of his sons Ishmael, and we find that in the Book of God in the story of The news about Abraham and what he was commanded to slaughter his son is that he is Ishmael, and that is because God said when he finished the story of the one of my sons who was slaughtered. Abraham said: {And We gave him good tidings of Isaac, a prophet from among the righteous.} Then he says: {So We gave her good tidings of Isaac, and after Isaac Jacob} He says: of a son. And the son of a son. So he was not commanded to slaughter Isaac, and he had been promised in it from God what He had promised him, and the one who commanded his slaughter was none other than Ishmael.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4039 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4040","So Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Abu Abdullah Al-Waqidi told us, he said: We disagreed regarding Ishmael and Isaac as to which of them Abraham wanted to slaughter, and where he wanted to slaughter it: in Mina or in the Holy House, so I wrote Whenever I heard of that from the hadith reports, Ibn Abi Sabra told me, on the authority of Abu Malik, one of the sons of the owner of the house, and he was a servant of Uthman. Ibn Affan, on the authority of Ata’ Ibn Yasar, who said: I asked Khwat Ibn Jubayr Al-Ansari about the sacrifice to God, which of the two was it? He said: Ishmael. When Ishmael was seven years old, Abraham saw in his sleep in his house in the Levant that he was slaughtering Ishmael, so he rode to him. On Buraq until he came to him and found him with his mother, so he took him by the hand and went with him as he was commanded to do, and Satan came to him in the form of a man he knew. He said: O Abraham, where do you want? Ibrahim said: “In my need.” He said: You want to slaughter Ishmael. Ibrahim said: “Have you seen a father slaughter his son?” He said: Yes, you. Ibrahim said: Why? He said: You claim that God commanded you to do that. Abraham said: “If God has commanded me, we will obey God and do well.” So he left him and came. Satan went to Hagar and said: Where did Abraham take your son? She said: He went to fulfill his needs.He said: He wants to slaughter him. She said: Have you seen a father slaughter his son? He said: He claims that God commanded him to do so. She said: He did well in that he obeyed God. Then he caught up with Ismail and said: O Ismail, where is Will your father take you? He said: Because of his need. He said: He is taking you to slaughter you. He said: Have you ever seen a father slaughter his child? He said: Yes, he said: Why? He said: He claims that God commanded him to do that. Ismail said: He did well in that he obeyed his Lord. He said: So he took him out until he ended up with him in Mina, where he He ordered, then he came to the slope of the body today, and said: “My son, God has commanded me to slaughter you.” Ismail said: So obey, for Obedience to your Lord is all good. Then Ismail said: Did you inform my mother of that? He said: “No.” He said: “You are right. I am afraid that you will be sad, but if you bring the knife close to my throat, turn away from me, for it is better for you to be patient.” And do not see me. So Abraham did so, so he made a slitting in his throat, and when the slitting was in some brass, the blade rubbed against him, so he sharpened it two or three times with the stone each. That cannot be upset. Abraham said: “Indeed, this command is from God, so he raised his head.”Then, behold, a ibex was standing before him, and Abraham said: “Arise, my son, for I have come to be sacrificed for you.” So he slaughtered it there in Mina. Al-Waqidi said: He told me Rabia bin Othman, on the authority of Hilal bin Osama, on the authority of Ata bin Yasar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Salam, that he said: “The one being sacrificed is Ismail.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4040 - What Al-Waqidi and Al-Sihah have"
"4041","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Zayd bin Al-Khabab told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Al-Ahnaf ibn Qais, on the authority of Al-Abbas ibn Abdul-Muttalib, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “He said The Prophet of God, David: O Lord, I hear the people saying: My Lord, Isaac said: Indeed, Isaac sacrificed himself for me. This is an authentic hadith that the people narrated on the authority of Ali. Ibn Zayd Ibn Jud’an was the only one with it.”"
"4042","Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Adl al-Saffar told me, Ahmad ibn Nasr told me, Amr ibn Hammad told me, Asbat ibn Nasr told me, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: Sarah was ninety years old, and Ibrahim was one hundred and twenty years old. A year later, when the terror had passed from Abraham and the good news of Isaac came to him, and he felt safe from those who feared him, he said: “Praise be to God who has given me The eldest of Ishmael and Isaac. Indeed, my Lord hears supplications. So Gabriel, peace be upon him, came to Sarah with good news, and said: “Give good tidings of a son who will be called “Ishaq, and after Isaac is Jacob.” He said: Then she struck her forehead in amazement. That is what God Almighty says: “So she hid her face” [Al-Dhariyat: 29] and said: I am giving birth and I am old and this is my husband who is old. This is a strange thing. They said: Are you amazed at the command of God? May God’s mercy and blessings be upon you, people. Indeed, it is Praiseworthy and Glorious. “Al-Bukhari used Ikrimah as evidence, and Muslim protested Al-Suddi, and the hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4042 - True"
"4043","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Ahmasi told me, Al-Hussein bin Humaid bin Muhammad bin Al-Rabi’ told us, Marwan bin Ja’far Al-Samri told us, Humaid told us Ibn Muadh, Mudarrak Ibn Abdul Rahman told us, Al-Hasan Ibn Dhakwan told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, on the authority of Ka’b Al-Ahbar, he said: “Then it was Ishaq bin Ibrahim, whom God made a light, shining and the apple of an eye for his parents. He was one of the people with the best face, the most beautiful, and the best of manners. Logically speaking, he was white, with curly hair and a beard, resembling Abraham in appearance and character, and to Isaac he fathered Jacob and Esez, so Jacob was The best of them, the most eloquent, the most beautiful and handsome, and Esas had a lot of hair on his head, body, and face, and he lived among the Romans.” Samurah bin Jundub narrated:
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4043 - Its chain of transmission is weak"
"4044","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mil narrated to us, Al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha’arani narrated to us, Sunayd ibn Dawud narrated to us, Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Dawud ibn Abi Hind, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, {And We gave him good tidings of Isaac} He said: “He was given good tidings of prophecy. He was given good tidings about him twice when he was born. “And when we were informed,” the chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4044 - True"
"4045","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Amr bin Abi Sufyan bin Usayd bin Jariyah told him that Ka’b said to Abu Hurairah: Shall I not tell you about Ishaq bin Ibrahim the Prophet,? Abu Hurairah said: “Yes.” Ka’b said: When Abraham saw that Isaac would be slaughtered, Satan said: By God, if I do not test it, then I will Abraham. I will never tempt any of them. Then Satan appeared to them as a man they knew. He said: So he approached, until Abraham came out with Isaac. To slaughter him, he went to Sarah, Abraham's wife, and said to her: Where did Abraham go to bring Isaac? Sarah said: He ate some of his needs in the morning. Satan said: No, by God, he did not dine in the morning for that. Sarah said: Why did he dine with him in the morning? He said: He brought him in the morning to slaughter him. Sarah said: And there is nothing in that. He would not have slaughtered his son. Satan said: Yes, by God. Sarah said: Why did he slaughter it? He said: He claimed that his Lord had commanded him to do so, so Sarah said: He had done well to obey his Lord if He had commanded him to do so. Then Satan came out from Sarah, until he caught up with Isaac as he was walking in the footsteps of his father, and said: Where did your father go? He said: He came with me in the morning to fulfill some of his needs.Satan said: No, by God, he did not go with you in the morning to satisfy some need, but rather he went with you in the morning to slaughter you. Ishaq said: My father would not have slaughtered me. He said: Yes, he said: Why? He said: He claimed that God commanded him to do that. Isaac said: By God, if He commanded him to obey him, then Satan left him and hurried to Abraham and said: Where You have become happy with your son. He said: I went out in the morning to fulfill some need. He said: No, by God, I did not go out with him in the morning except to slaughter him. He said: Why should I slaughter him? He said: You claimed that God commanded you to do that. He said: By God, if God had commanded me, I would have done it. He said: When Abraham took Isaac to slaughter him And he delivered Isaac, may God heal him, and ransomed him with a great sacrifice. Abraham said to Isaac: Arise, my son, for God has pardoned you, and God has inspired Ishaq: I have given you an invitation that I will respond to you. Ishaq said: I am calling upon you to respond to me, every servant of the first who meets you. And the others do not associate anything with You, so admit him into Paradise.” Al-Hakim said: “The context of this hadith is from the words of Ka’b bin Maati’ al-Ahbar, even if it appears There is a chain of narration in it that I judged to be authentic based on the conditions of the two Sheikhs, for this is an authentic chain of narration that is beyond doubt.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4045 - It is authentic and beyond doubt"
"4046","Ismail bin Ali Al-Khatbi told us in Baghdad, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Musa bin Ismail, and Hajjaj bin Minhal told us, they said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “He is Ishaq, meaning the sacrificed one.” Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khuthaym, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: “The one who wanted Abraham Isaac slaughtered him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4046 - True"
"4047","Ismail bin Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Sha’arani told us, Jeddi told us, Sunayd bin Dawud told us, Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, On the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: “The sacrificed Isaac.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4047 - Abu Dawud Sunayd said it was not like that"
"4048","Abu Abdullah bin Battah told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Muhammad bin Omar Al-Waqidi told us, Abu Suleiman Daoud told us. Ibn Abdul Rahman Al-Attar, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Uthman Ibn Khathim, on the authority of Saeed Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “Indeed, the rock that is at the root of Thubair, on which Abraham sacrificed Isaac, upon which a dusty ram landed, wailing like Thubair had lamented.” He narrated a long talk. Al-Waqidi said: Muhammad bin Amr Al-Uwaisi told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, who said: When Abraham saw in Dreaming that he would slaughter Isaac, he took his hand and reminded him of his greatness. Al-Hakim said: Al-Waqidi mentioned it with his chains of transmission, and this saying is on the authority of Abu Hurairah, Abdullah bin Salam and Umayr bin Qatada. Al-Laythi, Othman bin Affan, Ubayy bin Ka’b, Abdullah bin Masoud, Abdullah bin Omar, and Abdullah bin Amr, and God knows best. I used to see the sheikhs of hadith before us and in all the cities in which we sought hadith, and they did not disagree that the one being sacrificed was Ishmael. Their basis in it is the saying of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “I am the son of the two sacrifices,” since there is no dispute that he is from the descendants of Ishmael and that the other sacrifice His younger father was Abdullah bin Abdul Muttalib. Now, I find the compilers of this evidence choosing the statement of the one who said: It is Isaac. As for the narration on the authority of Wahb ibn Munabbih, which is the chapter of these sciences,"
"4049","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Isfaraini told us, Abu Al-Hasan bin Al-Baraa told us, Abd Al-Munim bin Idris told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Wahb bin Alarmingly, he said: The hadith of Isaac when God commanded Abraham to slaughter him, and God gave Abraham Isaac on the night the angels departed from him. When he was the son of seven, God inspired Abraham to slaughter it and make it an offering. At that time, the offering was accepted and taken away, so it was concealed. Abraham, that is Isaac and all the people, and he confided him to a friend of his, so he said, “The conqueror is the righteous, and he was the first to believe in Abraham,” and he said to him: Al-Siddiq: God does not put you to the test of someone like this, but He wants to test you and test you, so do not think badly of God, for God He will make you a leader for the people. There is no power or strength over Abraham and Isaac except in God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. So Wahb mentioned a long hadith until he said Wahb: And I was informed that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Ishaq preceded the people in a call to which no one had preceded him, and they will rise on the Day of Resurrection, let them intercede for the people of this call. And God approached Abraham in that place and said: Hear from me, O Abraham, O most truthful. The truthful, and he said to Isaac: Listen to me, O most patient of those who are patient, for I have afflicted you today with a great affliction that I have not afflicted anyone among my creation. I have tested you, O Abraham, with fire, and you have been patient with patience the likes of which no one in the world has been patient with, and I have tested you with striving for My sake while you were alone. And weak, so you were truthful and patient with patience and honesty the likes of which no one in the world had ever believed, and I tested you, O Isaac, with slaughter, and you did not hold back. yourself and did not glorify that in obedience to your father, and you saw that he was happy and small in the name of God, as one hopes for the best of his reward and is pleased with him. Meeting him, and today I make a covenant with you that I will not hold you back. As for you, O Abraham, Paradise has been destined for you for me, for you are my friend from Among the people of the earth, not among the men of the worlds, and it is a virtue that no one before you achieved, nor anyone after you. So Abraham fell down, prostrating in veneration of what He heard the words of God, giving thanks to God. As for you, O Isaac, grant me whatever you wish, ask me, and grant me your request. He said: I ask you, O My God, please choose me for yourself and make me intercede among your monotheist servants, so that no servant who does not associate anything with you will meet you except that you will protect him from the fire. He said: To him is his Lord: I have fulfilled for you what you have asked, and I have guaranteed for you your guardianship, as I have promised you upon myself, a promise that I will not break, a covenant from which I will not be held back, and a gift. “Congratulations, not bad.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4049 - Abdel Moneim bin Idris Nothing"
"4050","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl told me, Abu Ghassan Al-Nahdi told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Tamimi, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, his saying: {And when his Lord tested Abraham with certain words, and he fulfilled them} [Al-Baqarah: 124] He said: “The rituals of Hajj.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and there are many witnesses to it, which I have mentioned in the Book of Rites.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4050 - True"
"4051","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Isfaraini told us, Abu Al-Hasan bin Al-Baraa told us, Abd Al-Muneim told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Wahb bin Munabbih, He said: “When Sarah died, Abraham married a woman called Hajora, and she bore him seven sons: Bephes, Midian, Kesan, and Lot. And Sarkh, and Umaym, and Naashan. “And he also mentioned in this book Wahab: a lowly descendant of Abraham, and that Lot was one of them.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4051 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4052","Muhammad bin Ishaq al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Nasr told us, Amr bin Talha al-Qannad told us, Asbat bin Nasr told us, on the authority of al-Suddi, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “The Prophet’s Lot, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was the son of my brother Ibrahim Al-Khalil, peace be upon him.” This Authentic chain of transmission “And in the book of Ismail bin Abdul Karim, on the authority of Abd al-Samad bin Mughaffal, he said: I heard Wahb bin Munabbih saying: “He came out Abraham with his wife Sarah, and with her her brother Lot, to the land of the Levant.” And it is in a third saying.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4052 - True"
"4053","Abu Al-Hasan bin Shabawayh Al-Rais told us, narrated to us. . . . . . . . . . . Ibn Sasawayh, Muhammad bin Humayd told us, Salamah bin Al-Fadl told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, he said: “The Prophet’s Lot, may God bless him and grant him peace, is Lot bin Varan bin Azar bin Bakhur bin Akhi Ibrahim Al-Khalil and Al-Mutafaqa are the people of Lot.”"
"4054","Muhammad ibn Yaqoub and Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Musa al-Saydalani told us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ayyub informed us, Musa ibn Ismail informed us, Hammad told us. Bin Salamah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, in His Almighty saying: {or shelter} [Hud: 80] to A severe corner. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “May God have mercy on Lot. He used to stay in a severe corner, and God did not send a prophet after him except in Wealth from his people.” This is an authentic hadith according to Muslim’s conditions, and they did not include it with this addition. Rather, they agreed on the hadith of Al-Zuhri on the authority of Sa’id. And Abu Ubaid, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, briefly.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4054 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4055","Muhammad bin Ali al-San’ani told us, Ali bin al-Mubarak al-San’ani told us, Zaid bin al-Mubarak told us, Muhammad bin Thawr told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, {or a jackal To a severe corner} [Hud: 80] He said: “It has reached us that no prophet was ever sent after Lot except to seek wealth from his people.”"
"4056","Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saffar told us, Ahmad ibn Nasr told us, Amr ibn Talha al-Qannad told us, Asbat told us, on the authority of al-Suddi, he said: “Lot went off and came down against the people of Sodom, and he found them marrying men, so he descended among them, so God sent him to them, and he summoned them and admonished them, and from their experience was what God related in His book
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4056 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4057","Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Ahmasi told us, Al-Hussein bin Humaid told us, Humaid bin Muadh told me, Mudarrak bin Abdul Rahman told me, Hassan told us Ibn Dhakwan, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, on the authority of Ka’b Al-Ahbar, said: “Lot was a prophet of God, and he was the son of Abraham’s brother, and he was a man He has a white, beautiful face, a delicate nose, small ears, long fingers, good curves, the best of people when he laughs, and it makes him feel good. He made him calmer, wiser, and did the least harm to his people, even though he was informed of the great harm that they wanted upon him, on behalf of his people. He says: {If only I had strength over you or could take refuge in a strong corner} [Hud: 80]
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4057 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4058","Abu Abdullah bin Battah told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Al-Waqidi told us, he said: And we were informed that Abraham when He migrated to the land of the Levant, and they took him out of it as a fugitive, so he set off and Sarah with him, and she said to him: I have sacrificed myself, so God inspired him to He married her, and it was the first revelation that was sent down to him. Lot believed in him, in a group of his people with him, and he said: “I am migrating to my Lord. It is He.” The Mighty, the Wise, so they expelled him from the land of Babylon to the Holy Land until he reached Harran, then they expelled him from it until they were pushed to the Jordan and in it. A mighty man among the mighty, until God destroyed him. Then Abraham returned to the Levant and Lot with him. God informed Lot and sent him to the gatherings as a messenger. Calling to God. These are five cities, the largest of which is Sodom, then Amud, then Urum, then Saur, then Sabur, and the people of these cities were Four thousand thousand people, so Lot went down to Sodom and stayed among them for twenty-four years, commanding them and forbidding them and calling them to God and to Worshiping Him and abandoning the immoral and evil practices they were doing, and hospitality was required of Lot, just as it was required of Abraham. And Ishmael, his people did not host anyone, and they used to bring the males from among the worlds and invite the women, so God reproached them for that on the tongue of Their Prophet in the Qur’an, and he said: “Do you bring the two reminders from among the worlds and leave behind what your Lord has created for you of your wives?” [Al-Shu’ara’: 166] Wahb said: Abdullah bin Abbas mentioned that what prompted them to have intercourse with men and not women was that they had orchards and fruits in their homes. And orchards and fruits outside on the back of the road, and they were struck by severe drought and hunger, so they said to one another: If you withhold your fruits This was a phenomenon of the people of the Wayfarers, from which you had a livelihood, and they said: How do we prevent it? Then some of them turned to each other, and they said: Follow your Sunnah. In it, whoever you find in your country as a stranger whom you do not know, rob him, marry him, and take him away, for people will not set foot in your country if you do so. That is, Satan came to them on those mountains in the form of a bright boy, the most beautiful and beautiful boy the people had ever seen, so they baptized him, married him, and robbed him. They withdrew him, then he went away, and no one of the people would come to them unless they did something to him, and that was their practice, until God sent Lot to them, but Lot forbade them from doing so. Then he warned them of the torment and apologized to them, and said: O my people, you are committing an indecency that no one of the worlds has ever done before you. He mentioned the rest of the hadith on the authority of Ibn Abbas
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4058 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4059","Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Nasr told us, Amr bin Talha told us, Asbat told us, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Abu Malik, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, and on one occasion, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, and on the authority of some of the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a chain of transmission traceable to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “When I went out The angels went from Abraham towards the village of Lot and came to it at midday. When they reached the River Sodom, they found Lot’s daughter drawing water. To her family, and he had two daughters, so they said to her: O maid, is there a house? She said: Yes, do not enter your place until I come to you. So she came to her father and said: O my father, I see a young man at the gate of the city that I have not seen. The faces of a people are more beautiful than theirs. Your people do not take them and expose them. His people were so forbidden to host a man that they said: It is permissible. On us, let the men host. He came to them and did not inform anyone except the house of Lot’s family. Then his wife went out and informed his people. She said: “Indeed, there is a house in the house of Lot’s family.” Lot was a man whose faces I had never seen before. Then his people came running to him, and when they came, Lot said to them: “O my people, fear God and do not You are disgraced in My hospitality. Is there not a sensible man among you? These are my daughters. They are purer for you than what you want.” They said to him: Why do we not bother to entertain men? You know that we have no right over your daughters, and that you know what we want. So when they did not accept from him what he offered to them, he said: “If only I had you. strength, or take refuge in a harsh corner.” He, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, says: “If only I had supporters who would help me against you, or a clan that would protect me from you, there would be certain circumstances.” Between you and what you have come, you want him from my guests.” And when Lot said: “If only I had power over you or could hide in a strong corner, then Gabriel spread out.” With his wings, he gouged out their eyes and they went out, treading on each other's tracks, blind. They said: He saved, he saved, for in the house of Lot, a people was enchanted in Earth. That is the saying of God Almighty: {And they turned him away from his guest, so We obscured their eyes} [Al-Qamar: 37] And they said: O Lot, indeed, we are messengers of your Lord. They reach you, so go with your family at night, and none of you turn around except your wife, so follow in the footsteps of your family. He says: “And go Wherever you are commanded, God brought them out to the Levant.” And Lot said: They destroyed them at that hour, so they said: We were not commanded except to break the dawn. Is not the dawn near? So when If it was magic, Lot and his family left except for his wife, that is the saying of God Almighty: {Except the family of Lot, We saved them with magic} [Al-Qamar: 34] “This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4059 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4060","Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Hashimi told us, Ahmed bin Salamah, and Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told us, they said: Nasr bin Ali Al-Jahdami told us, My father told me, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr ibn Maymun, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: “Hud the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was a man “Flogging” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4060 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4061","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ghayath Al-Abdi told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Khaythamah told us, Ma’mal bin Ismail told us, Hammad bin Salamah, Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib narrated on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Sabit, who said: “No nation was destroyed without its Prophet joining Mecca, where he was worshiped.” Therein until he dies, and Hud’s grave is between Al-Hijr and Zamzam.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4061 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4062","Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Shabawayh, the chief of Marwa, told us, Ja’far bin Muhammad Al-Naysaburi told us, Mihran Al-Razi told us, Salamah bin Al-Fadl, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abi Saeed Al-Khuza’i, on the authority of Abu Tufayl Amer bin Wathilah, who said: I heard Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, said to a man from Hadhramaut: “Have you seen a red dune mixed with red mud and a lot of sidr trees?” In such and such direction? He said: By God, O Commander of the Faithful, you described him as you described a man who had seen him. He said: “No, but I told him about it.” Al-Hadrami said: What is the matter with him, O Commander of the Faithful? He said: “In it is the grave of Hud, may God bless him and grant him peace.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4062 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4063","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Isfaraini told us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Baraa told us, Abd Al-Munim bin Idris told us, on the authority of his father, he said: Wahb bin Munabbih was asked about Hud: Was he the father of the Yemen who was born to them? Wahb said: “No, but he is the brother of Yemen, and in the Torah he is attributed to Noah. When there was unrest among the Arabs and Mudar was proud of her father Ishmael, Yemen claimed Hud as the father, so that she would be a son of the prophets, and his descendants were among them, and he was not their father, but he was their brother, and rather he was sent to Aad, and Wahb did not name Aad, he described them, nor attributed the lineage of their tribes, nor did he command their people, and there was not on earth a nation more numerous. Of them in number, none greater in stature than them, nor more powerful than them, and when they saw the wind blowing upon them, they said to the Jews, “Do you frighten us with the wind?” So they gathered their descendants, their money, and their animals into a people, then they stood at the gate of that people, turning away the wind from their money and their families. Then the wind entered from under their feet between them and the ground until it uprooted them.” Wahb said: And when God sent Hud bin Abdullah bin Rabah ibn al-Harith ibn Aad ibn Uz ibn Iram ibn Sam ibn Nuh. Every sand that God placed in some part of the country was the dwellings of Aad in And the land of Ad was the most fertile of the Arab countries, and had the most countryside, rivers, and gardens. When God was angry with them, they turned away from God and were Owners of idols that they worship instead of God. God has sent upon them the destructive wind.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4063 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4064","Abu Saeed Al-Ahmasi told us, in Kufa, Al-Hussein bin Humaid bin Al-Rabi’ told us, Marwan bin Jaafar told me, Humaid bin Muadh told me, Mudrik told me, Al-Hasan bin Dhakwan told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, on the authority of Ka’b, he said: “The Prophet of God Hud was likened to Adam by people.” “Peace”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4064 - Its chain of transmission is weak"
"4065","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Yahya bin Ma’in told us, Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, On the authority of Nawf al-Shami, “The Prophet’s favor, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was among the Arabs when God destroyed ‘Ad and its affairs ended, and Thamud was populated after it. So they were appointed successors in the land and spread out, then they rebelled against God. When their corruption became apparent and they worshiped other than God, God sent to them a righteous man, and they were a people. Arabs, and he was one of the middle of them in lineage and the best of them in position, and their homes were Al-Hijr as far as Qar’, which is Wadi Al-Qura, eighteen miles away. Between Al-Hijr and Al-Hijaz, then God sent him to them as a young boy, and he called them to God until he became arrogant and arrogant, and none of them followed him except a few. They were oppressed, so Ad and Thamud perished, and whoever was among them from those nations, and they were from the descendants of Laod bin Shem bin Noah, but he was not among Noah. And Abraham was a prophet before him, that is, before Abraham, except for Hud and righteous.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4065 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4066","Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Ahmasi told me, Al-Hussein bin Humaid bin Al-Rabi’ told me, Marwan bin Jaafar told me, Humaid bin Muadh told me, Mudarrek told me, Al-Hasan bin Dhakwan, on the authority of Al-Hasan Al-Basri, on the authority of Samurah, on the authority of Ka’b, said: “Then Saleh was the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was He resembles Jesus, son of Mary. He is red to white, and he has the same plump head.”"
"4067","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Isfaraini told us, Abu Al-Hasan bin Al-Baraa told us, Abd Al-Muneim bin Idris told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Wahb bin Alarming, he said: The hadith of Salih bin Ubaid bin Jabir bin Thamud bin Jabir bin Sam bin Nuh. Wahb said: “Indeed, God sent Salih to his people.” When the dream came to an end, he was a man with red to white hair, with straight hair, and he was walking barefoot as Jesus, son of Mary, peace be upon them both, did not take He does not wear shoes, he does not paint, he does not take a house or a dwelling, and he remains with the camel of his Lord. Wherever it goes, he goes with it, and wherever it descends, it descends. With her, and he had fasted forty days before the she-camel was slaughtered, and there was a mole on his right hand as a sign, so he stayed with them for forty years. They call them to God from when he was a boy until he became an adult, and they only increase in transgression.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4067 - On the authority of Wahb with a weak chain of transmission"
"4068",""
"4069","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl told us, Jiddi told us, Musaddad told us, Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdullah, on the authority of Shahr bin Hawshab, on the authority of Amr bin Kharijah, said: We told him: Narrate to us the hadith of Thamud. He said: I am telling you on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of Thamud, and Thamud was a righteous people whom God provided for in this world, and he lived for a long time. their lives, until one of them built a tabernacle out of mud, and it collapsed while one of them was alive. So when they saw that, they took off from the mountains. They divided houses, carved them, carved them out, and hollowed them out, and they had enough of their livelihood, so they said: O righteous one, pray for us your Lord to bring out for us a sign that we will know. Indeed, you are the Messenger of God. So Salih called upon his Lord, and he brought out the she-camel for them. Her drinking was a day, and their drinking was a known day. So if it was a day When they drank it, they abandoned it and the water, and they milked the water from it, so they filled every vessel, bowl, and waterskin. So God revealed to Salih that your people They will slaughter your she-camel. He said to them, and they said: We would not do it. He said: “If you do not sterilize her, a child will soon be born among you who will sterilize her.” He said: What is the sign of that child? By God, we will not find him except We killed him. He said: “He is a blond, blue-red-haired boy.”He said: There were in the city two noble and powerful sheikhs. One of them had a son who was unwilling to marry, and the other had a daughter for whom he could not find a match. So he gathered There was a sitting between them, and one of them said to his friend: What prevented you from marrying your son? He said: I do not find a match for him. He said: My daughter is a match for him, and I will marry your son. So he married him off, and that child was born between them, and it was in The city is full of eight people who are making mischief on earth and are not reforming. Salih said to them: “It will only be ravaged by someone born among you.” So they chose eight. He brought women from the town and made a condition with them, so they would go around the town, and when they found a woman in labor, they would look at her child. If it was a boy, then they stayed to see what it was, and if it was a slave girl, they turned away from her. When they found that newborn, the women screamed, saying: This is what the Messenger of God, Salih, wants. The conditions wanted them to take him, so his grandfather came between them and him, and they said: If he is Salih, he wants this. We killed him, and he was the worst born, and he used to grow young during the day like the youth of others on Friday, and he would grow young on Friday like the youth of other people during the month, and he would grow old on Friday. One month is younger than it is in the year, so the eight who are making mischief on earth and are not reformers and the two old men gathered together.They said: We will use this boy as our employer because of his status and the honor of his grandparents. There were nine of them, and Salih did not sleep with them in the village, but He was in the wilderness in a mosque, which was called: A righteous mosque, where he spent the night. When morning came, he came to them and advised them and reminded them. One evening, he went out to spend the night and spent the night there. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “And when they wanted to plot against Salih, they walked until they came to He drank on a righteous path, and eight hid therein: And they said, “If he revolts against us, we will kill him and go to his people and lodge them.” So God commanded the earth. So she settled down over them, so they gathered and walked to the camel while she was standing on her lap. The wretched man said to one of them: Bring her, and he sterilized her. So he came to her. This made him grievous, so he refrained from that, so he sent another, and this made it grievous, so he did not send a man unless that grievanced him regarding her matter until He walked towards her and stepped forward and struck her in the hock, so she fell running, and a righteous man among them came and said: Find the she-camel, she has been hampered. So he came and they left. They will receive it, O Prophet of God: So-and-so made it promiscuous, at no fault of ours. He said: See whether you can catch its blood, but if you can catch it, perhaps God will The torment will be lifted from you, so they went out looking for it, and when the detachment saw its mother getting disturbed, it came to a mountain called Al-Gharah for a short while.So he ascended and they went to take him. Then God inspired the mountain and it flew into the sky until the birds could catch it. He said: “And Salih entered the town, and when The faction saw him crying until his tears flowed, then he greeted Saleh and foamed a foam, then another foam, then another foam, then Saleh said to everyone Enjoy the day in your home for three days. That is a promise that is not false. Except that the sign of torment is that the first day becomes Their faces were yellowish, the second day they were red, and the third day they were black. When they woke up, their faces were as if they had been painted with the creation. Young and old, male and female, when evening came, they all cried out, “A day of punishment has passed and the torment has come upon you.” When On the morning of the second day, their faces were red as if they were drenched with blood, and they shouted, raged, and wept, and they knew that it was torment, so when they reached the night, They all shouted out, “Two days of punishment have passed and the torment has come upon you.” When the third day came, their faces were blackened as if It was coated with pitch, and they all shouted, “The torment has come upon you.” They were shrouded and mummified, and their embalms were filled with aloes and myrrh, and their shrouds were covered with dirt.Then they threw themselves into the earth and began to turn their gazes to the heavens once and to the earth sometimes, not knowing where they were coming from. The punishment came from above them from the sky or from under their feet from the earth, out of humility and apprehension. When they became the fourth day, a shout came to them from the sky. Therein will be the sound of every thunderbolt and the sound of everything that has a voice on earth, and their hearts will be torn in their chests, and they will become crouched in their homes.” This A comprehensive hadith that mentions the destruction of the family of Thamud. It was reported only by Shahr ibn Hawshab and he has no chain of transmission other than it, and he did not dispense with narrating it and he has a witness to it. By way of brevity with a correct chain of transmission that indicates the authenticity of the long hadith according to the condition of a Muslim.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4069 - Abu Bakr bin Abdullah Wah"
"4070","Abu Bakr Ismail bin Muhammad Al-Zaafrani told us about Al-Ray, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Al-Faraj Al-Azraq told us, Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, he said: And he said Ibn Jurayj: Abu Al-Zubayr told us, he said: I heard Jabir bin Abdullah, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said when he came to the stone, he praised"
"4071",""
"4072","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Balawayh told me, Muhammad ibn Shadhan al-Jawhari told me, Sa`id ibn Sulayman al-Wasiti told me, Sharik ibn Abd told me. By God, on the authority of Samak ibn Harb, and Salem al-Aftas, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in the Almighty’s saying: {And indeed, we will see you among us. Weak} [Hud: 91] He said: “Shuaib was blind.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4072 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4073","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Isfaraini informed us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Baraa told us, Abd Al-Munim bin Idris told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Wahb Ibn Munabbih said: God sent Shuaib to the people of Midian, and they were the owners of a grove. The grove was made of a twisted tree, and they were the people of Disbelief in God, an understatement of the people in measures and weights, and a spoilage of their wealth, and God Almighty had expanded provision for them and made abundant for them. In life, he lured them in despite their disbelief in him, so Shuaib said to them: “O my people, worship God. You have no god other than Him, and do not diminish. The measure and the balance, I see you are fine, and I fear for you the torment of a terrible day. This was one of Shuaib’s words to his people and his response. “His people will have what God has mentioned in His Book.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4073 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4074","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Hasan bin Musa Al-Ashib told us, Saeed bin Zaid, brother of Hammad bin Zaid, Hatim bin Abi Saghira, Barir al-Bahili told me, he said: I asked Abdullah bin Abbas about the destruction of Shuaib’s people and God’s words to them, so He took them. The torment of the Day of Shadows: It was the torment of a great day. Abdullah bin Abbas said: “God sent upon them a severe heat that took their breath away.” So they entered the inner chambers of the houses, and He entered upon them the inner chambers of the houses and took their breath away, so they left the houses to flee into the wilderness, so God sent A cloud and shaded them from the sun, and they found therein coolness and comfort, so they called out to one another until, when they gathered under it, God sent fire upon them. Abdullah bin Abbas: “That is the torment of the Day of Shadow. Indeed, it was the torment of a great day.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4074 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4075","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Jarir bin Hazim told me that he heard Qatadah, He says: “God sent Shuaib, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to two nations, to his people, the people of Midian, and to the owners of the grove. The grove was one of A twisted tree. When God wanted to punish them, God sent a severe heat upon them and raised the torment upon them as if it were a cloud. When it approached them, they went out. He hoped for it to be cool, and when they were under it, it rained on them, and He said: That is the saying of the Almighty, “So the torment of the Day of Shade overtakes them.” [Al-Shu'ara: 189] """"
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4075 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4076","Abdul Rahman bin Al-Hasan Al-Qadi told me, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told me, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Warqa’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, in his saying: {The torment on the Day of Shadow} [Al-Shu’ara’: 189] He said: “Shadows of torment.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4076 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4077","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Dawud bin Qays Al-Farra’ told me, on the authority of Zaid bin I accept, in the words of God Almighty: {Your origins command you that we abandon what our fathers worshiped or that we do with our wealth whatever we please} [Hud: 87] He said: “It was something that forbade them from putting aside the dirhams, or he said cutting off the dirhams, so the torment of the Day of Shadow overtook them. It was the torment of the Day of Great, he said: God sent to them a canopy of clouds and God sent to the sun, and it was burned on the earth, so they all went out to that canopy until “When they all gathered together, God would remove the canopy over them and heat the sun over them, so they would be burned like locusts are burned in a frying pan.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4077 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4078","Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Sunni informed us about Marw, Abu Al-Muwajih informed us, Abdan informed us, Abu Hamza informed us, on the authority of Jabir, On the authority of Amer, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “Whoever of the scholars tells you about the torment of the Day of Shadows is a lie.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4078 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4079","Bakr bin Muhammad al-Sayrifi told us about Marw, Abd al-Samad bin al-Fadl told us, Khalaf bin al-Walid told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Simak bin Harb, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: “Jacob bin Ishaq bin Ibrahim is Israel, peace be upon them.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4079 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4080","Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saffar told me, Ahmad ibn Nasr told me, Amr ibn Talha told me, Asbat ibn Nasr told me, on the authority of al-Suddi, on the authority of Murrah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: “As for the tribes, they are the sons of Jacob: Joseph, Benjamin, Rubel, Judah, Simeon, Levi, Dan, and Phahat. They were Twelve men, of whom God raised up twelve tribes. No one knows their lineage except God Almighty. God Almighty said: {And We divided them into two Ten tribes, nations} [Al-A’raf: 160] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4080 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4081","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Ghasili told me, Al-Hussein bin Amr bin Muhammad Al-Anqazi told us, Ubayy told us, Asbat, on the authority of Al-Sadi, said: “Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Khalil married a woman, and she became pregnant with two boys in her womb. When she wanted to give birth, he fought. The two boys were in her womb, so Jacob wanted to come out before Essa, so Essa said: By God, if you come out before me, I will be separated in my mother’s womb. So we will kill her. So Jacob delayed and Essa went out before him. And Jacob took the heel of Essa and went out. So he was called Essa because he was a staff, and he was called Jacob, because he went out, taking Essa’s heel, and he was the larger of the two in the womb, but he disobeyed and went out before him, so the two young men grew older, and it was Essa. He loved them to his father, and Jacob loved them to his mother, and Essa was a hunter, and when Isaac grew up he became blind. He spoke at length.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4081 - Its chain of transmission is weak"
"4082","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, and Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib bin Harb, and Ishaq bin Al-Hasan bin Maimun, they said: Affan bin Muslim told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, Thabit reported, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Joseph and his mother were given half of the good deeds.” This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of Muslim, but they did not take it out.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4082 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4083","Makram bin Ishaq, the judge in Baghdad, told us, Ahmad bin Malaab bin Hayyan told us, Saeed bin Amir told us, Muhammad bin Amr bin Alqamah told us, On the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The Most Generous, the son of the Most Generous, the son of the Most Generous, the son of the Most Generous, Yusuf. “The son of Ya’qub, the son of Ishaq, the son of Abraham, the Prophet of God, the son of the Prophet of God, the son of the Prophet of God, the son of Khalil, God.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim. And they did not bring it out.”"
"4084","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, he said: Asma bin Kharijah came to the door of Abdullah bin Masoud and said: I am the son of the honorable sheikhs, so Abdullah bin Masoud: “That is Yusuf bin Ya’qub bin Ishaq bin Ibrahim.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4084 - True"
"4085","Abu Abdullah Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad told us, Hadba told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Yunus bin Ubaid, on the authority of Al-Hasan, “that Yusuf He, peace be upon him, was thrown into the pit when he was twelve years old, and he met his father when he was eighty.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4085 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4086","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmed bin Mahran told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Rabi’ah Al-Harashi, He said: “The good deeds were divided and half was given to Joseph and Sarah, and half to the rest of the people.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4086 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4087","Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Adl told me, Muhammad ibn Imran al-Nasawi told me, Ahmad ibn Zuhayr told me, al-Fadl ibn Ghanim told me, Salama ibn al-Fadl told me, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to me, on the authority of Ruh ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of Abu Harun, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he said, while describing Joseph when he saw him in the third heaven, he said: “I saw a man whose image was like the image of the moon on the night of the full moon, so I said: O Gabriel. Who is this? He said: This is your brother Joseph. Ibn Ishaq said: God had given Joseph more beauty and prestige than any other world. Before him, nor after him, to the point where it was said: And God knows best, he was given half of the good deeds and the other half was divided among the people.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4087 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4088","Ahmad bin Sahl al-Faqih told us in Bukhara, Saleh bin Muhammad bin Habib al-Hafiz told us, Ahmad bin Imran al-Ahmasi told us, Muhammad bin Fudayl, Yunus bin Abi Ishaq told us, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of Abu Musa, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, descended with a Bedouin and honored him, and said: He said to him: “O Bedouin, ask what you need.” He said: O Messenger of God, a she-camel on her mount and a goat that my family is milking. He said it twice, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Are you unable to be like the old women of the Children of Israel?” Then his companions said: O Messenger of God, and how old are the Children of Israel? He said: “Moses wanted to lead the Children of Israel, but he went astray from the path, so the scholars of the Children of Israel said to him: We tell you that Joseph took We have covenants from God that we will not leave Egypt until we carry his bones with us. He said: And which of you knows where Joseph’s grave is? They said: You do not know where his grave is Joseph, except the old man of the children of Israel, so he sent to her and said, “Show me the grave of Joseph,” and she said: No, by God, I will not do so until I am with you in Paradise. He said: “The Messenger of God disliked what she said, so it was said to him: Give her her ruling. So he gave her her ruling. She came to a lake and said: ‘Put this out.’” Water. When they had sacked him, she said, “Dig here.” And when they had dug, they saw the bones of Joseph. And when they had taken them up from the ground, behold, the road was as bright as daylight. A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”"
"4089","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Ahmasi told me in Kufa, Al-Hussein bin Humaid bin Al-Rabi’ told me, Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Sulami told me, Muhammad bin Hassan told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ja’far bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, who said: “The knowledge and wisdom of God were among the heirs of Abraham, so when That is what God gave to Joseph, the son of Jacob, king of the Holy Land, and he reigned for seventy-two years. That is what He said in what was sent down of His Book: You have given me kingdom and taught me the interpretation of hadiths} [Yusuf: 101] the verse “
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4089 - It is not valid"
"4090","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Ju’fi told us, Al-Fudayl bin Iyad told us, He said: “There were eighty years between the separation between Joseph and Jacob’s stone until they met.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4090 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4091","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Dinar al-Adl told us, Ahmad bin Nasr told us, Abu Nu`aym told us, Zuhayr told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, said: “Joseph was only bought for twenty dirhams, and his family when he sent to them while they were in Egypt were three hundred.” And ninety people, whose men are prophets and whose women are truthful ones. By God, they did not go out with Moses until they reached six hundred thousand and seventy thousand.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4091 - True"
"4092","Abu Saeed Al-Ahmasi told me, Al-Hussein bin Humaid told me, Marwan bin Ja’far Al-Samri told me, Humaid bin Muadh told me, Mudarrek bin Abdul Rahman, Al-Hasan bin Dhakwan told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, on the authority of Ka’b, who said: “Then Jacob was born, Joseph, the truthful one whom God chose And he chose him and honored him and divided for him two-thirds of the camels and divided a third among his servants, and he resembled Adam on the day God created him, formed him, and breathed There was part of his spirit in him before the sin befell him. When Adam disobeyed, the light, splendor, and goodness were taken from him, and God had given Adam the good. And beauty, light, and splendor on the day He was created. When he did what he did and committed sin, that was removed from him. Then God gave Adam a third of the camels. With the repentance that he repented for, then God gave Joseph the beauty, beauty, light and splendor that He took away from Adam when he committed the sin. This is because God loved for His servants to see that He is capable of whatever He wills, and He gave Joseph of goodness and beauty that He had not given to any other person. Then God gave him knowledge of the interpretation of the vision, and he used to tell him about the thing he had seen in his dream that it would happen, and before it happened God knew it. Just as He taught Adam all the names, and when he smiled, you saw light in his molars, and when he spoke, you saw a ray of light in his words and they burned. Inflammation between its folds.” I have summarized from the stories of Joseph, peace and blessings be upon him, what the path is clear to, even if I took into account the wonders of Wahb ibn Munabbih And Abu Abdullah Al-Waqidi, because it took a long time to translate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4092 - On the authority of Samra, on the authority of Ka’b, and the chain of transmission is weak"
"4093","Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Shabawayh, the chief of Marwa, told us, Ja’far bin Muhammad Al-Naysaburi told us, Ali bin Mahran told us, Salama bin Al-Fadl, Muhammad bin Ishaq told me, he said: “Moses bin Misha bin Joseph bin Jacob was born, and he prophesied among the children of Israel before Moses bin Imran, as they claim and those who are certain of it claim, that he was the one who asked the world to learn from him until he realized the scientist who had breached the ship, He killed the boy, built the wall, and Moses bin Misha was with him, then he departed from him until he reached what he had reached.”
 Al-Hakim said: This is how Muhammad bin Ishaq mentions and uses as evidence the proven and authentic hadith, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, He said: I told Ibn Abbas that Nawaf al-Bikali claims that Musa, the companion of al-Khidr, is not Musa bin Imran, the companion of the Children of Israel, but rather he is Musa. Another, and Ibn Abbas said: “The enemy of God has lied.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4093 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4094","Ubayy ibn Ka’b told us that he heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, say: “Musa ibn Imran stood up as a preacher to the Children of Israel.” The hadith With his height. This is a hadith narrated in the two Sahih books, but he only forced me to mention it because I neglected to mention it from the middle. As for Musa bin Imran the Kaleem"
"4095","Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman bin Hamdan al-Jallab told us about Hamdan, Abu Hatim Muhammad bin Idris al-Hanthali told us, Abdullah bin Dahir told us. Ibn Yahya Al-Razi, my father told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abaya Al-Asadi, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, saying: “The God says in His Book to Musa bin Imran {Indeed, I have chosen you over the people with My messages and with My words, so take what I have given you and be of those who are thankful} [Al-A’raf: 144] He said: {And We wrote for him on the Tablets of every thing an exhortation and an explanation of every thing} [Al-A’raf: 145] He said: Then Moses saw that all things had It was proven to him, just as you see that your scholars have proven everything to you, just as they prove it. When Moses reached the seashore, he met The scholar asked him to speak, and he acknowledged to him the virtue of his knowledge and did not envy him. Moses said to him, urging him: Shall I follow you on the condition that you teach me what You taught Rashid, then the scholar knew that Moses could not stand his company and could not be patient with his knowledge. So the scholar said to him: You cannot be patient with me. How? Be patient over what you have no knowledge of. Then Musa said to him while apologizing: You will find me, God willing, patient and I will not disobey you. He knew that Musa could not stand his company and could not be patient with people. He taught him and said to him, “Then if you follow me, do not ask me about anything until I tell you about it.” So they got into the ship, and the scholar broke it, and it was He broke it for God’s pleasure and for Moses’ displeasure, and he met the boy and killed him for God’s pleasure. “Then he mentioned some of the story and words, but Ibn Abbas did not go beyond this.” A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4095 - Abdullah bin Daher Al-Razi and his father are Rafidians"
"4096","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Yahya bin Ma’in told us, Yahya bin Adam told us, Hamza Al-Zayat told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Ubayy bin Ka’b, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “May God’s mercy be upon us and upon Moses,” so he began with himself, “If he had been patient, he would have told us of his story, but he said: If I ask you about anything after that, then do not You accompany me. You have received an excuse from me. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4096 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4097","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Isfaraini told us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Baraa told us, Abd Al-Munim bin Idris bin Sinan Al-Yamani told us, about His father, on the authority of Wahb bin Munabbih, said: “He mentioned the birth of Moses bin Imran bin Qahat bin Levi bin Jacob bin Ishaq bin Abraham And the hadith of God’s enemy Pharaoh when he was enslaving the children of Israel in his deeds in Egypt and the matter of Moses and Al-Khidr. Wahb said: And when Moses’ mother became pregnant Through Moses, she concealed her affair from all the people, so no one among God’s creation knew about her pregnancy, and that was something God pleased her with when He wanted to bestow His blessings upon her. Children of Israel, and when the year in which Musa bin Imran was born came, Pharaoh sent midwives, and he approached them and searched the women with an unparalleled search. They searched them before that. Moses’ mother became pregnant with Moses, but her womb did not grow, her color did not change, and her milk did not spoil, but the midwives Do not present it to her, for when the night came that Moses was born, his mother bore him, and there was no one watching over her or any one to attend, and no one saw her except her sister. Mary, and God inspired her to breastfeed him. Then, if you fear for him, throw him into the sea, and do not be afraid and do not be sad. Indeed, they will return him to you and make him The messengers.He said: So his mother kept him hidden for three months, breastfeeding him in her lap, neither crying nor moving. Then when she feared for him and for her, she made a sealed coffin for him. She made preparations for him in it, then threw him into the sea at night, as God had commanded her. The ark was made in the same way as the ships of the sea, five spans by five. It was great and could not be measured, so the ark came floating on the water, and the sea threw the ark onto the shore in the middle of the night. When Pharaoh rose in the morning, he sat in While he was sitting on the shore of the Nile, he saw the coffin, so he said to those of his servants around him, “Bring me this coffin,” and they brought it to him. When it was placed in his hands, They opened it and found Moses in it. He said: When Pharaoh looked at him, he said: However, I am one of the enemies. So that terrified him and angered him, and he said: How did he sin? This boy was slaughtered, and I had ordered the midwives not to conceal a child who was being born. He said: And Pharaoh had married a woman from the children of Israel. She was called Asiya bint Muzahim, and she was one of the best of the numbered women and one of the daughters of the prophets, and she was a mother to the Muslims who had mercy on them and gave alms. upon them and give it to them and they enter upon it,So she said to Pharaoh while she was sitting next to him: This newborn is older than a year old, and she only ordered the children to be slaughtered for this. The Sunnah, so let him be the apple of an eye for me and for you. Do not kill him on the chance that he will benefit us or that we will adopt him as a son while they do not feel that their destruction is at his hands. And Pharaoh had no children except daughters, so Pharaoh made him alive and exalted him, and God bestowed upon him His love, compassion, and mercy, and said: To his wife: Perhaps it will benefit you, but as for me, I do not want to benefit it. Wahb said: Ibn Abbas said: If the enemy of God had said about Moses as His wife said: Perhaps he will benefit us so that God will benefit him through him, but he refused the misery that God had decreed for him, and God forbade eight wet nurses for Moses. For days and nights, whenever a wet-nurse was brought to him and he would not accept her breast, Pharaoh and his mercy showed mercy to him and wet nurses were requested for him, and he mentioned a feeling of sadness. The mother of Moses and her weeping over him to the point that she was almost ready to kill him, then God dealt with her with His mercy and made her heart firm until the news of him reached her. So she said to his sister, “Disguise yourself and go with the people and see what they will do to him.” So his sister went in with the midwives to Asiyah bint Muzahim. When she saw They found them in Moses, their love for him, and their tenderness towards him.She said: Shall I direct you to the people of a household who will take care of him for you and be sincere to him until he was returned to his mother? Then Moses stayed with his mother until So she weaned him, then returned him to her, and Moses grew up in Pharaoh’s lap, with his wife raising him with their own hands, and they took him as a son, and while he played among Pharaoh's hands, and in his hand was a small, light rod that he was playing with. He raised the rod and struck Pharaoh with it on the head, and he looked at who had struck him until he was worried. By killing him, Asiya bint Muzahim said: O king, do not get angry and do not be harsh on you, for he is a young boy who does not understand. Try him if you wish. Put in this basin coal and gold, and see which of them will seize. So Pharaoh commanded that, and when Moses extended his hand to seize the gold. The king entrusted with him took his hand and returned it to the coal. Moses caught it and threw it into his mouth, then he threw it out when he found it was hot. Then Asia said to Pharaoh, “Did I not tell you that he does not understand anything, nor does he know it?” And Pharaoh desisted from him and believed her, but he ordered his death. It is said: The knot that was on Moses’ tongue was the effect of that ember that he bit.Wahb ibn Munabbih said: When Moses reached his maturity and reached forty years of age, God gave him knowledge, wisdom, and understanding, and he remained there for twelve years. Calling to the religion of Abraham and his laws, and to the religion of Isaac and Jacob, so a group of the children of Israel believed.” Then he mentioned the story in its length."
"4098","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Ahmad bin Yahya Al-Halwani told us, Muhammad bin Al-Sabbah told us, Ismail bin Zakaria told us, on the authority of Asim Al-Ahwal, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Indeed, God chose Moses By speech, and Ibrahim by kindness.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4098 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"4099","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Abu Abdullah Al-Bushangi told us, Musaddad bin Mashad told us, Al-Mu’tamir bin Sulayman told us, On the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Ka’b Al-Ahbar, he said: “Indeed, God Almighty has decreed His vision and His words.” Between Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Moses, and Muhammad saw him twice, and Moses spoke to him twice.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4099 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4100","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Ali bin Al-Hasan told us, Abu Zafar Abdul-Salam bin Mutahhar told us, Ja’far bin Suleiman told us, On the authority of Thabit al-Bunani, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Musa bin Imran is the friend of God.” This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”"
"4101","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Jallab narrated to me, Ahmad ibn Bishr al-Marthadi narrated to me, Yahya ibn Ma’in narrated to me, Hajjaj narrated to me, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Abu Al-Huwaith Abd al-Rahman bin Muawiyah said: “Moses stayed for forty days after God spoke to him, and no one would see him unless he died.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4101 - Its chain of transmission is soft"
"4102","Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Adl told me, Ahmad ibn Nasr told me, Amr ibn Talha al-Qannad told me, Asbat ibn Nasr told me, on the authority of al-Suddi, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that Moses bin Imran, when his Lord spoke to him, loved to look at it, so he said: My Lord, show me Look at you, he said: “You will not see me, but look at the mountain, and if it stays in its place, you will see me.” Then the angels surrounded the mountain, and surrounded He surrounded the angels with fire, and surrounded the angels around the fire, and surrounded the angels with fire, then your Lord was revealed to the mountain, then He was revealed from it like his little finger, and caused the mountain to collapse.” Moses fell down in shock, God willing, then he woke up and said: Glory be to You, I have turned to You in repentance, and I am the first of the believers, meaning the first. Whoever among the Children of Israel believed: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4102 - True"
"4103","Bakr bin Muhammad bin Hamdan Al-Sayrifi told us about Marw, Abd Al-Samad bin Al-Fadl told us, Khalaf bin Al-Walid Al-Jawhari told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Amr ibn Maimun, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, he said: “The tree in which Moses took shelter was mentioned to me. The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. I went to her for two days and two nights, then I woke her up in the morning, and she was green and lush, so I prayed for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted, and I greeted, and my camel yearned for it while he was hungry, and he took some of it from it while he was hungry, but it consumed it and he was not able to feed it. Then he said it, so I prayed for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and left.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4103 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4104","Ismail bin Ali Al-Khutami told us in Baghdad, Ismail bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Khuza’i told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, On the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited this verse: “And when his Lord appeared to the mountain, He made it Dhaka} [Al-A’raf: 143] “Hammad pointed and placed his thumb on the knuckle of his little finger and said: The mountain broke apart.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and it was not He brings him out.”"
"4105","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub and Ibrahim bin Asma told us, saying: Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, God willing - Abu Salamah doubted Musa bin Ismail - {Then when his Lord was manifested He made the mountain flattened.} [Al-A’raf: 143] He said: “He flattened the mountain.” Abu Ali Al-Hafiz narrated to us. Al-Hasan bin Sufyan and Imran bin Musa informed us. Al-Jurjani and Ahmad bin Ali bin Al-Muthanna said: Hadba bin Khalid narrated to us, Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us similar to the hadith of Al-Khuza’i and there is no doubt about it. Fringe
 Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Isfaraini informed us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Baraa told us, Abd Al-Munim bin Idris told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Wahb Ibn Munabbih said: Harun Ibn Imran had an eloquent tongue and was well-spoken. He spoke slowly and spoke with knowledge and forbearance, and he was taller than Moses. Long and the oldest of the two in age, and the thickest of the two in flesh, and the whitest of the two in body, and the largest of the two in planks, and Moses was a wrinkly man, and he was tall. As if he was one of the dishonorable men, and God did not send a prophet unless he had the mole of prophethood on his right hand, unless he was our prophet. Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, because the mole of prophecy was between his shoulders, and our Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was asked about that and he said: “This The mole between my shoulders is the mole of the prophets before me, because there is no prophet or messenger after me.”"
"4106","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Ahmasi told us, Al-Hussein bin Humaid told us, Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Sulami told us, Muhammad bin Hassan told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Jafar, on the authority of his father, said: “God’s knowledge and wisdom were in the descendants of Abraham, and then God gave Joseph bin Jacob, king of the earth.” He reigned for seventy-two years, and that is the saying of the Almighty: {My Lord, You have given me dominion and taught me the interpretation of hadiths, Fatir. The heavens and the earth} the verse. Then God sent Moses and Aaron and gave them inheritances from the easts and wests of the earth and made them a smooth kingdom. So Moses and those with him of the Children of Israel reigned for eighty-eight years, and then God Almighty wanted to restore that to them, so he made them king. the earth and its western parts, and gave them a great kingdom until they asked to look at their Lord, and they said: Show us God openly. That was when they saw Moses. His Lord spoke to him and they listened and asked for the vision, and Moses had chosen their choice so that they would bear witness for him before the Children of Israel that his Lord had spoken to him, so they said: We will not bear witness to you until you show us God plainly.” Then the thunderbolt took them while they were looking."
"4107","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, Ammar bin Abi Ammar told us, he said: I heard Abu Hurairah, saying: The Messenger of God said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Indeed, the Angel of Death used to come to the people visually, so he came to Moses bin Imran, and Moses slapped him and gouged out his eye, so the Angel of Death came back.” He said: O Lord, your servant Moses did such-and-such to me, and had it not been for his honor toward you, I would have been displeased with him. So God said, “Give my servant Moses and give him the choice between He places his hand on the back of a bull, and he has a year between him and every hair shown on his palm, and there is now a choice between him and his death. So he came to him and gave him a choice. Then Moses said: Then what? That? He said: Death. He said: Now then, he smelled him and took his soul, and God restored his sight. After that, he used to go to people in secret. An authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4107 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4108","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Isfaraini informed us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Baraa told us, Abd Al-Munim bin Idris told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Wahb Ibn Munabbih said: God mourned for Aaron for Moses when God wanted to take him to death. When he mourned for him, he was sad, and when he was taken, he was greatly distressed and wept. He cried for a long time, and when he returned to that, God Almighty came to him, consoling him and admonishing him, and said to him: “O Moses, you should not have longed for... You have nothing to do with me, and you are not to be comforted by anyone else, nor are you to pull your knees except through me, and you are not now worried about Aaron except for me, and how? Are you longing for some of the things while you hear my words? Or how are you longing to lose something of the world after I have chosen you with my messages? And with my words, and he mentioned a long monologue, he said, and Aaron and Moses, who were one hundred and seventeen years old, were arrested three years before the end of the wandering. And Aaron was arrested when he was one hundred and twenty years old. Moses remained after him for three years until he completed his one hundred and twenty years, and the children of Israel They are divided over it, they unite over it one time, and they disperse the other time.”"
"4109","Muhammad bin Ishaq al-Saffar al-Adl told us, Ahmad bin Nasr told us, Omar bin Talha al-Qannad told us, Asbat bin Nasr told us, on the authority of al-Suddi, in a report He mentioned it on the authority of Abu Malik, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of Murrah al-Hamdani, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Masoud, and on the authority of people from Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “Indeed, God revealed to Moses bin Imran, ‘Aaron has died, so bring him such-and-such mountain.’ So Moses set off.” And Aaron was near that mountain, and behold, they came to a tree that resembled it with a built house, and behold, they were in it with a bed with mattresses on it, and behold, in it A pleasant smell. When Aaron looked at that mountain and the house and what was in it, he admired it and said: O Moses, I would love to sleep on this. The bed. Moses said to him: So sleep on it. He said: I fear that the lord of this house will come and be angry with me. Moses said to him: Do not be afraid, I will suffice for you, the Lord of this house. So sleep, so he said: O Moses, sleep with me, for if the Lord of this house comes, he will be angry with me. And upon you all, when Aaron fell asleep, death took hold of him, and when he found his senses, he said: O Moses, you have deceived me. So when he died, that house was taken away, and that woman went away. The tree and the bed was raised to the sky. When Moses returned to the children of Israel and Aaron was not with him, they said: Moses killed Aaron and was envious of his love for the children of Israel. Israel is his, and Aaron was kind to them and gentler to them than Moses, and Moses was somewhat harsh towards them, so when he heard that, he said To them: Woe to you, he was my brother. Did you think that I should kill him? When they attacked him, he stood up and prayed two rak’ahs, then he called on God and descended on the bed until they looked at him between the heaven and the earth and believed him. “This is an authentic hadith.” On the condition of a Muslim, and they did not produce it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4109 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4110","Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Muhammad bin Shadhan Al-Jawhari told us, Saeed bin Suleiman told us, Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, in His Almighty saying: {O you who Believe, do not be like those who harmed Moses, but God cleared him of what they said} [Al-Ahzab: 69] He said: “Moses and Aaron ascended the mountain, and Aaron died, so the sons of Israel to Moses: You killed him. He was more loving toward us than you and more gentle toward us than you. So they harmed him in that, so God commanded the angels to carry him. So they passed him by the gatherings of the children of Israel until they learned of his death, so they buried him, and nothing recognized his grave except the marble. Indeed, God had made him deaf and dumb. A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4110 - True"
"4111","Abu Al-Hasan bin Shabawayh told us, Abu Al-Fadl Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Al-Harith told us, Ali bin Mihran told us, Salamah bin Al-Fadl told us, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Ishaq said: “Safy Allah Musa hated death and venerated it, but when he hated it, God loved that death should be made endearing to him and that he should hate it.” Life, so the prophecy was transmitted to Joshua bin Nun, and he would go to him in the morning and go, and Moses would say to him: O Prophet of God, what has God spoken to you? Then he would say To him, Joshua bin Nun: O Prophet of God, have I not accompanied you for such-and-such a year? Was I asking you about something of what God has told you so that you may be You are the one who initiates it and remembers it. When Moses saw that, he hated life and loved death.”"
"4112","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Isfaraini informed us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Baraa told us, Abd Al-Munim bin Idris told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Wahb Ibn Munabbih said: “It was mentioned to me that it was related to the death of Safi Allah Musa, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he was only staying in a shelter and eating.” And he would drink from a waterhole made of stone, just as an animal would dig into that waterhole, out of humility before God, until God honored him with what He honored him with through His words, and he was one of The matter of his death is that one day he left his throne for some need, and no one among God’s creation knew, so he passed by a group of angels digging A grave, so he recognized them and approached them until he stood over them. Suddenly they were digging a grave, and he had never seen anything better than it as what was in it. Green, fresh, and joyful. Then he said to them: O angels of God, for whom are you digging this grave? They said: We are digging it for a servant, by God Generous to his Lord, so he said: This servant of God is in a dwelling that I have never seen resting or entering in like today. That was when he received from God what He has presented in He seized it, and the angels said to him: O my friend of God, would you like to be that? He said: I wished, so they said: Come down, lie down in it, and face yourself. To your Lord, then he breathed the easiest he had ever breathed, so he descended and lay down in it and turned to his Lord, then he breathed and God took his soul, then The angels prayed for him, and God’s friend Moses, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was ascetic in this world and desiring the Hereafter.”"
"4113","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Amr Al-Ahmasi told me, Al-Hussein bin Humaid bin Al-Rabi’ told me, Marwan bin Jaafar Al-Samari told me, Humaid bin Muadh told me, Mudarrak bin Abdul Rahman told me, Al-Hasan bin Dhakwan told me, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Abi Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah bin Jundub, On the authority of Ka’b, may God be pleased with him, he said: “Job, son of Amoz, was the patient prophet of God, whom Satan, the enemy of God, brought against him with his soldiers and horses. And his husband to tempt him and remove him from the remembrance of God, so God protected him, and Satan found no way to him, so God bestowed tranquility on Job. And patience in the face of his affliction with which He afflicted him, so God called it {What an excellent servant, indeed he is steadfast} [p. 44], and Job was a tall man with curly hair and broad hair. He had good eyes and a good disposition. On his forehead was written “the afflicted and patient.” He had a short neck, a broad chest, and thick legs and forearms. He used to give Widows and clothing them, striving and sincere to God Almighty.” Al-Hakim said: “They disagreed about Ayyub, as to what time he was sent, so Wahb ibn Noting: He is one of the descendants of Abraham after Joseph, and Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Yassar said: Someone I do not accuse told me about Wahb that he is Ayyub ibn Amuz bin Razzah bin Isa bin Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Khalil, and Muhammad bin Jarir mentioned that he was before Shuaib, and Abu Bakr bin Khaythamah, because he was after Suleiman bin Dawud, and God knows best.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4113 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4114","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told me, Musa bin Ismail told me, Hammad bin Salamah told me, Ali bin Zaid told me, about Yusuf bin Mihran, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that Ayyub’s wife said to him: “And God has brought down upon me hardship and poverty.” As soon as my people sent a loaf of bread and I fed you, pray to God to heal you. He said: Woe to you. We were in bliss for seventy years, but we are in calamity for seven years. """
"4115","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid told us dictation, Ahmad bin Mihran told us, Shuaib bin Al-Hakam bin Abi Maryam told us, Nafi’ bin Yazid, Aqeel bin Khalid told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “Indeed, Job, the Prophet of God, remained in his affliction for fifteen years, and he was rejected by those near and far, except for two men from his brothers who were among the most distinguished. His brothers, they used to go to him in the morning and go, and one of them said to his friend one day: We know, by God, that Job has committed a sin. No one among the worlds has committed a sin and his companion said to him: What is that? He said: For eighteen years, God did not have mercy on him, so he revealed what was wrong with him. When he went to Ayoub, the man was not patient until he mentioned it to him. Then Job said to him: I do not know what you are saying except that God knows that I was passing by two men disputing, remembering God, so I returned to my house. So I will make amends for their hatred of remembering God except in a proper manner, and he used to go out for his needs, and when he fulfilled his needs his wife would hold him by the hand. Until he reached puberty, then one day he slowed down for her, so God inspired Job in his place, “Run with your foot. This is a cold bath.” And a drink, so she lingered and picked him up and he approached her. God had removed his affliction, and he was the best he had ever been. When she saw him, she said: That is, God bless you. Have you seen this afflicted Prophet of God? By God, for that reason, I have never seen a man more like him than you, when he was authentic. He said: “For I am he.” He said: “And he had two strangers.” for wheat and scarcer for barley, so God sent two clouds, and when one of them was the scarcest of wheat, it emptied gold into it until it overflowed and emptied The other is in the rarest paper barley until it overflows: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4115 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4116","Abu Sa`id Ahmad ibn Ya`qub al-Thaqafi told us, Muhammad ibn Ayyub told us, and Abu Muslim and Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Hafs told us: Amr ibn Hafs told us: Marzouq, Hammam told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of An-Nadr ibn Anas, on the authority of Bashir ibn Nahik, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: When God healed Job, He rained locusts of gold upon him, and he began to take them in his hand and place them on his garment. It was said to him: O Job, did you not Are you satisfied? He said: Who can be satisfied with your mercy? “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4116 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4117","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Adawi told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Abu Hilal told us, on the authority of Qatada, he said: “He was afflicted with Job spent seven years in charge of the sweeping of the Holy House.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4117 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4118","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Isfaraini informed us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Baraa told us, Abd Al-Munim bin Idris told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Wahb Ibn Munabbih said: “Ayoub was ninety-three years old, and upon his death he bequeathed to his son Hamal, and God sent his son after him. He gave glad tidings to Ibn Ayyub as a prophet, and he named him Dhul-Kifl, and commanded him to pray for his monotheism, and that he was residing in the Levant, his entire life until he died, and he was He was seventy-five years old, and Bishr bequeathed to his son Abdan, then God sent Shuaib after them.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4118 - In its chain of transmission is Abd al-Moneim bin Idris, and he lied."
"4119","Abu Saeed Al-Ahmasi told me, Al-Hussein bin Humaid bin Al-Rabi’ told me, Marwan bin Ja’far told me, Humayd bin Muadh told me, Mudarrek bin Abdul Rahman, Al-Hasan bin Dhakwan told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, on the authority of Ka’b, who said: “Then Elias, the Prophet of God, was a companion of mountains and wilderness. He would be alone there, worshiping his Lord. He had a large head, a short belly, and narrow legs, and he had a red mole on his head. But God raised him to the rank of The land of the Levant, and he was not taken up to heaven, so Elisha bequeathed the prophethood after him.”"
"4120","Abu Saeed Al-Ahmasi told me, Al-Hussein bin Humaid told me, Marwan bin Jaafar told me, Humaid bin Muadh told me, Mudarrek bin Abd told me. Al-Rahman, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Dhakwan, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, on the authority of Ka’b, may God be pleased with him, who said: “And Yunus bin Matta, whom God named Dhul-Nun, and he said: {And Dhul-Nun, when he went away in anger, he thought that We would not defeat him, so he called out in the darkness: There is no god but You. Glory be to You. I was of the wrongdoers.} [Al-Anbiya’: 87] So God responded to him and saved him from the grief of three darknesses: the darkness of the night, the darkness of the sea, and the darkness of the belly. Pisces, and spent the night over his people and sent him to a hundred thousand or more, and they believed, so God granted them enjoyment until their appointed times which He had decreed for them, but He did not He will destroy them with torment.”"
"4121","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Sulayman bin Abi Daoud Al-Burnisi told us, Muhammad bin Ubaid Al-Tanafisi told us, Yunus bin My father Ishaq Al-Subai’i, Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Sa’id bin Abi Waqqas narrated to me, my father Muhammad narrated to me, on the authority of his father Sa’d, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “The supplication of Dhul-Nun which he supplicated in the belly of the whale: There is no god but You, Glory be to You. Indeed, I have been of the wrongdoers. No Muslim has supplicated with it.” In distress, God responded to him. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4121 - True"
"4122","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq narrated to me from the origin of his book, Ali bin Al-Hussein bin Al-Hamid narrated to us, Al-Mu’affa bin Sulaiman narrated to us, Fulayh bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Hilal bin Ali, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yassar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever says: I am better than Yunus ibn Matta lied: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it with this wording.” Rather, they agreed on the hadith of Abu Al-Aliyah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas No one should say: “I am better than Yunus bin Matta.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4122 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4123","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Affan bin Muslim, and Abu Salama told us, they said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, Dawud informed us Ibn Abi Hind, on the authority of Saeed Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by Thaniya and said: “What is this?” They said: The second of such-and-such, and he said: “It is as if I were looking at Yunus ibn Matta riding a camel with a fibre-like muzzle, and he was wearing a robe of wool, and he was saying: At your service, O God, at your service. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4123 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4124","Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Adl told me, Ahmad ibn Nasr told me, Amr ibn Talha told me, Asbat ibn Nasr told me, on the authority of al-Suddi, On the authority of Abu Malik, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “Yunus stayed in the belly of the whale for forty days.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4124 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4125","Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told me, Muhammad bin Shazan told me, Saeed bin Sulayman told us, Abu Hamza Al-Attar told us, he said: I heard Al-Hasan, and he was asked Regarding the words of God Almighty: {And had he not been of those who glorify God} [Al-Saffat: 143] He said: “He would have prayed abundantly during the Du’aa’.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4125 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4126","Abu Saeed Al-Ahmasi told me, Al-Hussein bin Humaid told us, Othman bin Muhammad told us, Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, Sharik bin Abdullah told us, about Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi: “Indeed, Yunus ibn Matta was bitten by a whale and he sacrificed and died in the evening.”"
"4127","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Mughaffal Al-Muzani told me, Ahmed bin Najda Al-Qurashi told me, Yahya bin Abdul Hamid told us, Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Kathir ibn Zaid, on the authority of Al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab, on the authority of Mus’ab ibn Sa’d, on the authority of Sa’d, may God be pleased with him On his authority, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever supplicates with the supplication of Jonah, which he supplicated in the belly of the whale, will be answered.” This is evidence of what he preceded."
"4128","Abu Muhammad al-Isfaraini told us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Baraa told us, Abd al-Muneim ibn Idris told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Wahb: “ Yunus, son of Matthew, was a righteous servant and there was distress in his character, so when the burdens of prophecy were burdened upon him, and there are burdens that only a few can bear So it disintegrated under it, just as a quarter disintegrated under a burden, so he threw it out of his body and escaped from it, the Almighty said to his Prophet Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings be upon him: {So be patient as those of resolve among the messengers were patient} {So be patient for the judgment of your Lord, and do not be like the companion of the whale when he called out while he was distressed} [The Pen: 48] That is, do not meet another as he met him.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4128 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4129","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl Al-Sha’arani told me, Jeddi told me, Sunayd bin Dawud told us, Ja’far bin Suleiman told me, about the Bedouin’s affliction, on the authority of Al-Hasan, said: “When Yunus fell into the belly of the whale, he thought it was death, so he moved his legs, and behold, they were moving, so he prostrated and said: O Lord, I have taken “You have a mosque in a place where no one has ever prostrated.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4129 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4130","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Isfaraini told us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Baraa told us, Abd Al-Munim bin Idris told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Wahb Ibn Munabbih, he said: “The Prophet of God was David Ibn Isha Ibn Obed Ibn Baar Ibn Salmon Ibn Hasun Ibn Yarab Ibn Ram Ibn Hadron Ibn Pharez Ibn Yehuda Ibn Jacob Ibn Ishaq Ibn Ibrahim Al-Khalil, and he was a short man with blue hair, with sparse hair, a pure heart and a jurist.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4130 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4131","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, he said: Abdul Rahman bin Zaid bin told me He converted to Islam, on the authority of his father, in the words of God Almighty: {Have you not seen those who went out from their homes, and they were thousands, fearing death} [Al-Baqarah: 243] to His saying: {And God is All-Knowing of the wrongdoers} [Al-Baqarah: 95] He said: “God Almighty revealed to their Prophet that among so-and-so’s son is a man with whom God will kill Goliath and His sign is this horn. You put it on his head, so he will catch what he missed. So he came to him and said: God has revealed to me that among your children is a man who will kill God. With it, Goliath said: Yes, O Prophet of God. He said: So twelve men brought out for him like poles, and among them was a man who was adept at them, so he began to display them. On the horn and he did not see anything. He said: Then he said: Indeed, you have children other than these. He said: Yes, O Prophet of God, I have a short child whom I am ashamed for people to see. So I put him among the sheep. He said: Where is he? He said: He is in such-and-such a people. He said: So he went out to him and said: This is him, there is no doubt about him. He said: So he put the horn on his head and he stood up.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4131 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4132","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid told us, Ahmed bin Mahran told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Hisham bin Saad told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “When God created Adam, He wiped his back Then from his back came every breath of which He is the Creator, from his descendants until the Day of Resurrection, and He placed between the eyes of every human being a gleam of their light. Then he presented them to Adam and said: Which of these, my Lord? He said: These are your descendants. He said: Then he saw a man among them that he admired, and a gleam between his eyes said: O Lord, who is this? He said: This is a man from the last of the nations of your descendants, called David. He said: O Lord: How long have you made his lifespan? He said: Sixty years. He said: O Lord, increase forty years from my life. He said: Then it will be written and sealed and not changed. Then when Adam’s life had ended, an angel came to him. Death said: Did I not have forty years left of my life? He said: Did you not give it to your son David? He said: He denied, so his descendants denied, and he forgot, and I forgot. His descendants made a mistake, so his descendants made a mistake. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4132 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4133","Abu Saeed Al-Ahmasi told us, Al-Hussein bin Humaid told us, Ibn Numayr told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, he said: “And Moses To David five hundred and sixty-nine years.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4133 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4134","Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saffar al-Sulami told me, Ahmad ibn Nasr told me, Amr ibn Talha al-Qannad told me, Asbat told me, on the authority of al-Suddi, in Al-Suddi said: “And We strengthened his kingdom” [p. 20]. David had divided the period into three days. A day in which he spends judgment among the people, and a day in which he is alone for his worship, and a day in which he is alone with his wives, and he had ninety-nine wives. And it was in what he read of the books that he used to find the virtue of Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob, so when he found that in what he read of the books, he said: Oh My Lord, I see all the good that my forefathers who were before me did, so give me what you gave them, and do to me what you did to them. He said: So God revealed to him: Your fathers were tested with trials that you were not tested with. Abraham was tested with the slaughter of his son, and Isaac was tested with the going. His sight, and Jacob was afflicted with his grief over Joseph, and you were not afflicted with anything from that. He said: O Lord, afflict me with the same as you afflicted them with. And give me the same as what you gave them. He said: Then God revealed to him: You are afflicted, so beware. He said: So he stayed after that as long as God wished that he should stay. When Satan came to him, taking the form of a golden dove, until it fell between his legs while he was standing and praying, he said: So he extended his hand to him to take it. So he flew out of the window, looked at where it was, and followed it. He said: Then he saw a woman washing on her roof, and he saw one of the most beautiful women. Then she turned around and saw him, then she threw back her hair and covered herself with it, and that increased his desire for her. He said: So he asked about her. Then he was informed that she had a husband and that her husband was absent with the weapon of such-and-such. He said: So he sent for the owner of the weapon and ordered him to He would send him to his enemy such-and-such. He said: So he sent him and he opened the door for him. He continued to send him until he was killed the third time and he got married. His wife, and when he entered upon her, he only remained for a short time until God sent to him two angels in the form of human beings. They asked to enter upon him, and they found him in On the day of his worship, the guards prevented them from entering upon him, so they surrounded the mihrab over him. He said: He did not feel it while he was praying when he had them in his hands. They were sitting, he said: Then he was frightened by them, so they said: Do not be afraid, we are only adversaries, some of us have wronged each other, so judge between us with justice, and do not be unjust. He says: “Do not be afraid.” And he mentioned the hadith at length in his acknowledgment of his sin.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4134 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4135","Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Ahmasi told me, Al-Hussein bin Humaid told me, Al-Hussein bin Ali told me, Muhammad bin Hassan told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Jaafar. Ibn Muhammad, on the authority of his father, who said: “God chose for his prophecy and for his message David Ibn Isha, so God gathered for him that light and wisdom.” And the Psalms increased it from him, so Dawud bin Isha reigned for seventy years, and he treated the people fairly with one another and decided to separate them according to what he had taught him. God gave him of His wisdom, and our Lord commanded the mountains and they obeyed Him, and He made iron for them, God willing, and our Lord commanded the angels to bear He has the ark, and David continued to manage with God’s knowledge and light, decreing what was lawful and forbidding what was unlawful, until, when God wanted, He would take it to Himself. It was inspired to him, “I entrust the light and wisdom of God, both apparent and hidden, to your son Solomon, son of David,” and he did so.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4135 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4136","Abu Bakr Al-Shafi’i told me, Ismail bin Ishaq told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Wahib told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi: In His saying, the Almighty, the Majestic: {And indeed We wrote in the Psalms after the remembrance} [Al-Anbiya’: 105] He said: In the Psalms of David after the remembrance of Moses {Indeed, the earth My righteous servants will inherit it.} [Al-Anbiya’: 105] He said: “Paradise.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4136 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4137","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told us, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad bin Al-Musayyab told us, dictation signed by Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq. Bin Khuzaymah, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir Al-Hazami told us, Husayn bin Zaid bin Ali told us, Shihab bin Abdul Rabbo told me, on the authority of Omar bin Ali bin Al-Hussein, he said: I walked with my uncle Muhammad bin Ali bin Al-Hussein to Jafar and said: The people claimed that Suleiman bin Dawud asked his Lord to grant him A kingdom that no one should have after him, and that it was the twenty. He said: I do not know what people say, but my father Ali bin Al-Hussein told me about His father, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “God has not given a long life to a king in the nation of a prophet who passed before him as long as that prophet reached the age of His nation
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4137 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4138","Ali bin Issa told us, Yahya bin Zakaria bin Dawud told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad al-Muharbi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, On the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Murrah, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, in His Almighty saying: {And David and Solomon when they judged the field, when The people’s sheep sprouted therein. He said: “A vineyard whose clusters sprouted and the sheep spoiled it.” He said: So David ruled for the sheep to the owner of the vineyard. Solomon said: Other than this, O Prophet of God. He said: What is that? He said: You give the vineyard to the owner of the sheep, and he takes care of it until it goes back to how it was. And you give the sheep to the owner of the vineyard, and he gets some of it until... The vineyard returned to what it was. You gave the vineyard to its owner, and you gave the sheep to its owner. God Almighty said: {Then We made it understandable to Solomon, and to each of us We gave wisdom and knowledge} [Al-Anbiya’: 79]
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4138 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4139","Abu Saeed Al-Ahmasi told us, Al-Hussein bin Humaid told us, Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Sulami told us, Muhammad bin Hassan told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Jafar Ibn Muhammad, on the authority of his father, said: “Solomon Ibn David was given the kingdom of the east and west of the land, and Solomon Ibn David reigned for seven hundred years.” For six months, He ruled over all the people of the world, including jinn, humans, devils, animals, birds, and wild animals, and was given knowledge of all things. And the logic of all things, and in his time wondrous works were created that people had never heard of, and they were subjected to him, and he did not cease to manage by the command of God and His light. And his wisdom, so that when God wanted to take him, He inspired him to entrust the knowledge and wisdom of God to his brother, and the sons of David, and they were four. One hundred and eighty men without a mission.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4139 - This is invalid"
"4140","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, said: “The Banu Ishaq dated from the sending of Moses to the reign of Solomon, son of David. He said: And Solomon inherited David. He said: The prophecy was given to him.” The message is to grant him a kingdom that no one after him should have, so He subjected to him the jinn, the humans, the birds, and the wind.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4140 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4141","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari told us, Abu Abdullah al-Bushanji told us, Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, Hajjaj told me, on the authority of Abi Ma’shar, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka’b, said: “We have learned that Suleiman bin Dawud had a army of one hundred farsakhs, twenty-five of which were for humans. And twenty-five for the jinn, and twenty-five for the beast, and twenty-five for the birds, and he had a thousand houses of bottles on wood. Of these, three hundred were open, and seven hundred were secret. So he commanded the stormy wind and it raised it, so he commanded the wind and it carried it, so God inspired him as he was walking between heaven and earth. Indeed, I have increased your dominion, lest any of the creatures speak anything except the wind comes and informs you.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4141 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4142","Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Al-Fadl told us, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad Al-Qabbani told us, Salam bin Junada Al-Qurashi told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, On the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “Sulaiman bin Dawud used to have six One hundred chairs, then the human nobles will come and sit from the next to them, then the jinn’s nobles will come and sit from the next to the human nobles, Then he calls for the birds and they give them shade, then he calls for the winds and they carry them away. He said: So in the single morning he will travel a month’s journey.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4142 - True"
"4143","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl Al-Bajli told us, Ismail bin Aban Al-Azdi told us, Yahya bin Zakaria told me Bin Abi Zaida, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Abdullah Al-Wadi’i, who said: I heard Mu’awiyah saying: “The king of the earth Four: Suleiman bin Dawud, Dhul-Qarnayn, a man from the people of Helwan, and another man. He was told: Al-Khidr? He said: “No.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4143 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4144","Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Sulami told us, Ahmad bin Nasr told us, Amr bin Hammad bin Talha Al-Qannad told us, Asbat bin Nasr told us, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Murrah, and Abu Malik, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, and on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Murrah, on the authority of Abdullah, they said: “There was another Prophets of the Children of Israel: Zechariah bin Adan bin Muslim, who was from the descendants of Jacob, said: “He will inherit my kingdom, and he will inherit prophecy from the family of Jacob.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4144 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4145","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Harun bin Sulaiman Al-Asbahani told us, Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit Al-Bunani, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Zechariah was a carpenter.” This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4145 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4146","Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saffar told me, Ahmad bin Nasr told me, Amr bin Talha told us, Asbat bin Nasr told us, on the authority of Al-Sadi, on the authority of Abu Malik, And Abu Salih, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, and on the authority of Murrah al-Hamdani, on the authority of Abdullah, said: “Zechariah called upon his Lord secretly and said: Lord I am weak in my bones, and my head is covered with gray hair, and I was not wretched in supplicating to you, my Lord, and I feared the followers behind me, and they were the group. My wife is barren, so grant me from Yourself a heir who will inherit me and inherit my prophecy and inherit from the family of Jacob. He will inherit the prophecy of the family of Jacob and make him a satisfied Lord. And His saying: Grant me from Yourself good offspring. His descendants say: You are the Hearer of supplications. And he said: My Lord, do not leave me alone, for You are the best of heirs. Then the angels called him, and it was Gabriel, and he was standing and praying in the sanctuary. “God gives you good news of a boy whose name is Yahya. We have not made for him anyone.” He accepted a name, before whom no one had been named Yahya. And the angels said: God gives you good news of Yahya, confirming a word from God, confirming Jesus and only a few. The limited: the one who does not want women. When he heard the call, Satan came to him and said to him: O Zechariah, the voice that you heard is not from God, but rather it is from Satan ridiculed you, even if it had been from God. He had revealed it to you just as he reveals to you any other matter. Then he was in doubt and said: How can I have a boy who will say, “Where is he from?” It will be that old age has reached me and my wife is barren. He will say: Thus does God do whatever He wills, and I created you before, and you were nothing. This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4146 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4147","Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Musa, the judge in Bukhara, informed us. Muhammad ibn Ayyub informed us. Musa ibn Ismail informed us. Ja`far informed us. Bin Suleiman Al-Dabai, on the authority of Abu Imran Al-Juni, on the authority of Nawf Al-Bikali, he said: Zachariah called on his Lord and said: “{My Lord, grant me offspring from You.” You are the Hearer of supplications. [Al Imran: 38] {Indeed, some of my bones have weakened, and my head has burned with gray hair.} [Maryam: 4] The verses, then he said: {How can I have a boy when she was My wife is barren, and I have reached the age of arrogance.} [Maryam: 9] He said, “Thus said your Lord, ‘It is easy for me. I created you before, and you were not a thing.’ He said My Lord, make for me a sign. He said, “Your sign is that you do not speak to people for three nights at a time.” He said: So he sealed his tongue for three days and their nights, while he was healthy and did not speak. {Then he came out to his people from the sanctuary, and inspired to them that they should glorify God in the morning.} [Maryam: 11] And in the evening, O Yahya, take the Scripture firmly, and We gave him the judgment. A child of the signs until {he will be raised up alive} [Maryam: 15]
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4147 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4148","Muhammad bin Hamdoun Al-Warraq told me, Ali bin Saeed Al-Askari told me, Al-Fadl bin Ghanim told us, Salama bin Al-Fadl told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, He said: “Zakaria and Imran had married two sisters, so Yahya’s mother was with Zakaria and Maryam’s mother was with Imran, so Imran and his mother perished. Maryam was pregnant with Maryam while she was a fetus in her womb, and they were, as they claim, God withheld the child from her until she gave birth, and they were the people of a household of God is in a place”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4148 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4149","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Affan told us, and Abu Salamah said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Habib bin The martyr, Yunus bin Ubaid, and Humaid, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Ali bin Zayd, on the authority of Yusuf bin Mahran, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “There is no human being who has not sinned or intended to commit a sin or committed it, unless it is Yahya ibn Zakariya.” “He was not concerned about any sin, nor did he commit it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4149 - Its chain of transmission is good"
"4150","Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Ahmasi told me, in Kufa, Al-Hussein bin Humaid told me, Marwan bin Jaafar told me, Humaid bin Muadh told me, Mudrak bin Abdul Rahman told me, Al-Hasan bin Dhakwan told me, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, on the authority of Ka’b, may God be pleased with him, who said: “Yahya was Ibn Zakaria was a gentleman and a reserved man. He did not approach women nor lust after them. He was a young man with a beautiful face and figure, soft wings, and short hair. Fingers, long nose, close eyebrows, precise voice, abundant in worship, strong in obedience to God.”"
"4151","Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Thaqafi told me, Muslim bin Junada told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, he said: “Jesus ibn Maryam and Yahya ibn Zechariah mentioned twelve thousand disciples teaching the people. He said: What they forbade them from was marrying one’s brother’s daughter. He said: And it was Their king had a niece whom he admired and wanted to marry, and she had a need for him every day. When her mother heard about this, she said to her: When you go to the king and he asks you what you need, say, “My need is for you to sacrifice Yahya bin Zakariya for me.” When she came in to him, he asked her what she wanted, and she said: My need is to slaughter Yahya bin Zakariya. He said: Ask me something else. She said: I only ask you for this. He said: When she refused, he called Yahya. The son of Zakariya called for Batsht, and he slaughtered him, and a drop of his blood dripped onto the ground and continued to boil until God sent Bukhtar to defeat them, and it came to him. An old man from among the children of Israel, and she directed him to that bloodshed, and God put it into his heart to kill for that bloodshed of them until he calmed down. So he killed seventy thousand. Some of them were from the age of one until he settled down: “This is an authentic hadith whose chain of narration is on the condition of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4151 - It has been mentioned and it is according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4152","So Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shafi’i told us from the origin of his book, Muhammad bin Shaddad Al-Musma’i told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Abdullah told us Ibn Habib Ibn Abi Thabit, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Sa’id Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “God revealed to Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace. Indeed, I killed seventy thousand people with Yahya bin Zakariya, and I will kill seventy thousand and seventy thousand with your daughter’s son.” He narrated it. Humaid bin Al-Rabi’ Al-Khazzaz, on the authority of Abu Nu’aym"
"4153","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Surayj bin Al-Nu’man Al-Jawhari told us, Fulayh bin Suleiman told us, on the authority of Hilal Ibn Ali, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Ibn Abi Amra, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I The people closest to Jesus, son of Mary, in this world and the hereafter. The prophets are brothers, their mothers have different fathers, and their religion is the same, and there is nothing between me and them. “Jesus, son of Mary, is a prophet.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4153 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4154","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Sulayman bin Harb told us, Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Habib, on the authority of Shahr bin Hawshab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: “Hannah gave birth to Mary, and Mary gave birth to Jesus.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4154 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4155","Ali bin Muhammad al-Qadi told me, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told me, Al-Hussein bin Amr Al-Anqazi told me, my father told me, Israel told me, on the authority of Jabir, On the authority of Zaid Al-Ammi, he said: “Jesus, son of Mary, was born on the day of Ashura.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4155 - Its chain of transmission is weak"
"4156","Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saffar al-Adl told me, Ahmad ibn Nasr told me, Amr ibn Hammad told me, Asbat told me, on the authority of al-Suddi, on the authority of Abu Malik, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, and on one occasion, on the authority of Abdullah, they said: “Mary went out to the side of the mihrab with her menstruation, and when she She was purified when she had a man with her, and this is His saying: {Then We sent to her Our Spirit, and he appeared to her as a perfect human being} [Maryam: 17], and this is Gabriel to him. She was terrified by him and said: “I seek refuge in the Most Gracious from you, if you are pious.” [Maryam: 18] He said: “I am only the messenger of your Lord to give you a boy.” Purified} [Maryam: 19] Verse, so she went out wearing her robe, so he took hold of her sleeve and blew into the pocket of her armor, and it was torn in front of her, so she entered. The murmur in her chest made her pregnant, and her sister, the wife of Zechariah, came to her one night to visit her. When she opened the door for her, she kept herself away from her, and a woman said: Zechariah: O Mary, did you feel that I was pregnant? Then Mary said again: I feel that I am with child.Then Zechariah’s wife said: Indeed, I found what was in my womb prostrating to what is in your womb. That is what God Almighty says: “Confirming a word from God.” [Al Imran: 39] Then Zachariah’s wife gave birth to Yahya, and when it was time for Mary to give birth, she went out to the side of the sanctuary, and labor brought her to a full body. The palm tree said out of shyness before the people: “I wish I had died before this and been forgetful and forgotten” [Maryam: 23] Then Gabriel called to her {from beneath her, Be sad. Your Lord has placed a light under you and has shaken to you the trunk of the palm tree, and it will cause fresh, fresh dates to fall on you.} [Maryam: 25] So she shook him and he ran to her in the The sanctuary is a river, and the secret: the river, and the palm tree dropped fresh, fresh, and when she gave birth to it, Satan went and told the children of Israel that Mary She gave birth, and when they wanted her to speak, she pointed to Jesus, and Jesus spoke and said: I am the servant of God. He gave me the Book and made me a prophet and made me blessed. So when Jesus was born. There was not an idol left on earth that was worshiped other than God except that it fell, prostrating before His face. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not take it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4156 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4157","Ali bin Issa told me, Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Azhari told me, Ali bin Hajar told me, Ali bin Mushar told me, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, on the authority of Jabir, that a delegation from Najran came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they said: What do you say about Jesus, son of Mary? He said: “He is the Spirit of God and His Word and the servant of God and His Messenger.” They said to him: May we curse you that he is not like that? He said: “And that is more beloved to you?” They said: Yes. He said: “If you wish.” Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came and gathered his sons, Al-Hasan, and Al-Hussein, and their leader said: Do not curse this man. By God, if you curse him, one of the two parties will certainly be defeated. So they came and said: O Abu Al-Qasim, our foolish people only wanted to curse you, and we would like for you to pardon us. He said: “I have pardoned you.” Then he said: “Indeed, “The torment has affected Najran.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4157 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4158","Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha’arani told me, my grandfather told me, Abu Thabit Muhammad ibn Ubaidullah al-Mada’ani told me, Ismail told me Bin Jafar, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Qusayt, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And he said: “Every child of Adam, Satan, received that stab from him, and for it the newborn begins screaming, except for Mary and her son, for her mother When she gave birth to her, meaning her mother, she said: I seek refuge with you and her offspring from the accursed Satan. Then he struck the veil without her and stabbed her in it, so he kissed her. He raised her with good acceptance, and made her grow a beautiful plant, and her mother perished, so he took her to her paternal maternal aunt, Umm Yahya. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and it is not He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4158 - True"
"4159","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Muhammad bin Saeed bin Al-Asbahani told us, Hussein bin Ali told us, On the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Maysarah, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “So they will come Jesus through intercession, and he says: Do you know anyone who is the word of God and His Spirit and heals the blind and the leper and raises the dead other than me? They say: No, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4159 - True"
"4160","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Hisham bin Ali told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Dawud bin Abi Al-Furat told us, Alba bin Ahmar told us, On the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The best women in the world are Khadija bint Khuwaylid and Fatima bint “Muhammad, Maryam bint Imran, and Asiyah bint Muzahim, Pharaoh’s wife.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it with this wording.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4160 - True"
"4161","Abu Al-Tayyib Muhammad bin Muhammad Al-Shairi told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, Jarir bin Hazim told us, Muhammad bin Sirin told us, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Only three people spoke in the cradle, Jesus, son of Mary, and one witness. Yusuf, the companion of Jurayj, and the son of Mashhatah, the daughter of Pharaoh. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4161 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4162","Abu Al-Tayyib Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Hayri told me, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab told us, Ya’la bin Ubaid told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Sa’id Ibn Abi Sa’id Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Ata’, the client of Umm Habibah, said: I heard Abu Hurairah saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Let Jesus, son of Mary, come down as a just arbiter and a just Imam, and let him walk as a pilgrim, or a performer of Umrah, or with their daughters, and they will come to my grave.” Until he greets me and I will return to him.” Abu Hurairah says: “That is, my nephews, if you see him, say: Abu Hurairah greets you.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not produce it in this context.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4162 - True"
"4163","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Dinar Al-Adl told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah and Al-Hasan bin Al-Fadl told us, they said: Affan bin Muslim, Hammam told us, Qatada told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Adam, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The The Spirit of God, Jesus, son of Mary, is descending upon you, and when you see him, recognize him. He is a square man, red and white, with two garments knitted as if His head is dripping, and if no wetness hits it, he strikes the cross, kills the pig, imposes the tax, calls the people to Islam and is destroyed. In the time of the Antichrist, God will bring security to the people of the earth until lions graze with camels, tigers with cows, and wolves, with... Sheep and the children play with the snakes, do not harm them. He remains for forty years, then he dies and the Muslims pray over him. This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4163 - True"
"4164","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Isfaraini told us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Baraa told us, Abd Al-Munim bin Idris told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Wahb bin Alarming, he said: “God caused Jesus, son of Mary, to die three hours during the day when He raised him to Himself, and the Christians claim that He caused him to die seven hours from the day. day, then revived it.” Wahb said: “The Christians claimed that Mary gave birth to Jesus, three hundred and sixty-three years had passed from the time of her birth.” Alexander, and they claimed that the birth of Yahya ibn Zakariya was six months before the birth of Jesus, and they claimed that Mary became pregnant with Jesus. She was thirteen years old, and that Jesus lived until he was taken up, being thirty-two years old, and that Mary remained after his taking up for six years, so it was Her entire lifespan was fifty-six years, and Zakaria bin Barchiah, the father of Yahya bin Zakaria, they claimed, was two hundred years old, and Maryam’s mother was pregnant with Maryam. When Mary was born, Zechariah took care of her after the death of her mother, because her paternal aunt, her mother’s sister, was with him, and the name of Mary’s mother was Anna, daughter of Faqud. Ibn Qayel” Al-Hakim said: “The narrations differed regarding the number of messengers among the prophets and other prophets, which was led to by ijtihad on the part of Adam until our Prophet, the Chosen One, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sent. I have mentioned them.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4164 - Abdel Moneim bin Idris has fallen"
"4165","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Isfaraini told us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Baraa told us, Abd Al-Munim bin Idris told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Wahb Ibn Munabbih, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, that he said to a man sitting with him while he was talking to his friends: Come closer to me, and he said The man told him: May God keep you, and by God, it is not good for me to ask you as these people asked, so he said: Come closer to me and I will tell you about the mentioned prophets. In the Book of God, I will tell you about Adam, that he was a ploughman, and I will tell you about Noah, that he was a carpenter, and I will tell you about Idris. He was a tailor slave, and I will tell you about David, that he was a gardener slave, and I will tell you about Moses, that he was a shepherd slave, and I will tell you about Abraham, that he was an agricultural slave, and I tell you about Salih, that he was a merchant slave, and I tell you about Solomon, that he was a slave whom God gave The king, and he used to fast six days at the beginning of the month, three days in the middle, and three days at the end, and he had nine hundred A secret, and three hundred Fahriyah, and I will tell you about the virgin’s son, Jesus, son of Mary, that he did not hide anything for the morrow, and he would say: The one who had lunch with me will provide me with dinner, and the one who had dinner with me will provide me with lunch. He worships God all night, prays until the sun rises, and during the day he travels, and fasts. “And I tell you about the chosen Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he used to graze the sheep of his family in Ajyad. He used to fast, so we would say: He would not break the fast, and he would break the fast, so we would say: He would not fast, and all of these are things we saw him fasting, and he would fast three days every month, and he would He has the softest wings of mankind, the best of knowledge, and the longest of knowledge.” And I tell you about Eve, that she used to spin the hair and twist it with her hand. So she clothed herself and her child, and that Maryam bint Imran used to do that. Al-Hakim said: “As for the hadith with the high chain of transmission that indicates The sentence is interpreted, so he is the one.”"
"4166","Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Al-Fadl bin Idris Al-Samiri told us in Baghdad, Al-Hasan bin Arafa bin Yazid Al-Abdi told us, Yahya bin Saeed Al-Saadi Al-Basri, Abdul-Malik Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Ubaid Ibn Umair Al-Laythi, on the authority of Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with him, he said: I entered upon The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in the mosque, so I took advantage of his solitude, and he said to me: “O Abu Dharr, the mosque has a greeting.” I said: And what His greeting, O Messenger of God? He said: “Two rak’ahs,” so I performed them, then he turned to me and said: O Messenger of God, you commanded me to pray, so what is prayer? He said: “The best place, so whoever wishes, less, and whoever wishes, more.” I said: O Messenger of God, which deeds are most beloved to God? He said: “Belief in God.” Then he mentioned the hadith until he said: So I said: O Messenger of God, how many prophets are there? He said: “One hundred thousand and twenty-four thousand prophets.” I said: How many of them are messengers? He said: “Three hundred and thirteen,” and he mentioned the rest of the hadith.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4166 - Al-Saadi is not trustworthy"
"4167","Abu Aoun Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Mahan the butcher in Mecca told us, Ali Al-Saffar told us, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali bin Zaid told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir Al-Hazami, Ibrahim bin Al-Muhajir bin Mismar told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, and Safwan bin Sulaym, on the authority of Yazid Al-Raqashi, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sent after eight thousand of the prophets from among them. Four thousand children of Israel.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4167 - Ibrahim and Yazid Wahiyan"
"4168","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Abu Al-Muthanna Al-Anbari told me, Yahya bin Mu’in told us, Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Abu al-Wadak, on the authority of Abu Sa`id, said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I am the seal of a thousand or more prophets.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4168 - Weak Mujalid"
"4169","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Muslim, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that he said: “Seventy prophets wearing woolen garments embarked upon the dawn of souls. Seventy prophets prayed in the Mosque of Al-Khaif.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4169 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4170","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya the Martyr told us, Abu Al-Rabi’ Suleiman bin Daoud told us. Al-Zahrani, Muhammad bin Thabit told us, Ma’abad bin Khalid Al-Ansari told us, on the authority of Yazid Al-Raqqashi, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “There were eight thousand prophets without my brothers among the prophets, then there was Jesus, son of Mary, then I was after him
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4170 - Its chain of transmission is weak"
"4171","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Ibrahim bin Saad, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ikrimah, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “He presented The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, Medina and the Jews say: This world is only seven thousand years.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4171 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4172","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Ahmad al-Faqih told us in Bukhara, Saleh bin Muhammad bin Habib al-Hafiz told us, Ibrahim bin al-Hajjaj al-Sami told us, Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Yusuf bin Mahran, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “The age of Adam was one thousand years.” Ibn Abbas said: “And between Adam and Noah a thousand years, and between Noah and Abraham a thousand years, and between Abraham and Moses seven hundred years, and between There are five hundred years between Moses and Jesus, and between Jesus and Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, six hundred years. Al-Hakim said: “I have presented the correct narration about... The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that there was no prophet between him and Jesus.” News was narrated about Khaled ibn Sinan and his daughter who entered upon The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his saying: “You are the daughter of my brother, a prophet who has been neglected by his people.”"
"4173","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih and Ja’far bin Muhammad Al-Khalidi told us, saying: Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Mu’alla bin Mahdi told us, Abu Awanah, on the authority of Abu Yunus, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that a man, from Banu Abs, called Khalid ibn Sinan, said To his people: I will extinguish from you the fire of Hadathan. He said: Then Amara bin Ziyad, a man from his people, said to him: By God, you never told us, O Khaled. Except really, what is the matter with you and with the fire of the two young men whom you claim to be extinguishing? He said: So he set off, and Amara bin Ziyad set off with him on the thirty of His people until they came to her as she emerged from the cleft of a mountain in Harra, which is called Harra Ashja’. Then Khaled made a plan for them and made them sit there. He said: If I delay you, do not call me by my name. So she came out like blond horses following one another. He said: So Khalid met her. So he struck her with his stick, saying: “It seemed, it seemed, it seemed all calm.” The son of the shepherd of the goats claimed that I would not leave her with my hands in my hands until he entered. With it is the split. He said: So he delayed them. He said: Then Amara bin Ziyad said: By God, if your companion were alive, he would have come out to you yet. They said: Call him. In his name,He said: So they said: He forbade us from calling him by his name, so they called him by his name. He said: So he went out to them, holding his head, and said: Didn’t it? I forbid you from calling on me by my name. By God, you have killed me, so bury me. When donkeys pass by you with a mutilated donkey, search for me, for you will find me. Alive, he said: So they buried him, then the donkeys passed by them with a mutilated donkey in it, so we said: Exhume it, for he commanded us to exhume it. Amara bin Ziyad said: Do not speak of Mudar. We are digging up our dead, and by God, we will never dig them up. He said: He had told them that there is in you His wife has two tablets, so if any matter is in doubt for you, look into them, for you will see what you are asked about. And he said: A menstruating woman should not touch them. He said: When they returned to his wife, they asked her about them, and she took them out while she was menstruating. He said: So he went with what was in them of knowledge. He said: So he said Abu Yunus: Samak bin Harb said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about him, and he said: “That is a prophet who was lost by his people.” Abu Yunus said: Samak said Ibn Harb: Ibn Khaled Ibn Sinan came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: “Welcome to my nephew.” Al-Hakim said: “This is an authentic hadith subject to the condition Al-Bukhari and did not narrate it.Abu Yunus is the one who narrated on the authority of Ikrimah, Hatim ibn Abi Saghira, and they all used him as evidence, and Al-Bukhari cited everything as evidence. It is authentic on the authority of Ikrimah, but as for the death of Khalid ibn Sinan like this, there is disagreement about it. I heard Abu Al-Asbagh Abd al-Malik ibn Nasr, Abu Othman Saeed bin Nasr, and Abu Abdullah bin Saleh Al-Maafiri, the Andalusians and their group, whom I trust, mention: “Between them and Kairouan is a sea, and in the middle of it is a great mountain, which no one can climb, and that their way is through the sea on the mountain, and that they They saw at the top of the mountain, in a cave, there a man covered in white wool, covered in white wool, with his head on his hands, as if he was sleeping and had not changed. There is something from him, and the people of the area testify that he is Khalid bin Sinan, and God Almighty knows best.”"
